+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:155](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L155) — **D-08 Viewports and per-view scale** — Independent scales measure correctly in exported PDF. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A sheet carries up to twelve viewports with independent view, level, scale and position, and resizing the paper refits frames without altering viewport scales (`src/studio/architect/authoredSheetSet.ts`). Export is real vector PDF (`sheets.ts`). Remaining: measuring an exported PDF at each declared viewport scale has not been executed.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:156](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L156) — **D-09 Drawing revisions and supersession** — Old revision remains retrievable and visibly superseded. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-12). Implemented: issue sets record immutable historical issue records and frozen sheet layouts with deterministic SHA-256 layout hashing and design revision tracking (`src/studio/architect/issueHistory.ts`, `model.ts`, `ArchitectSheets.tsx`). When a new revision is issued (e.g. Rev B), prior current issues automatically transition to `superseded` status with timestamps and pointers to the successor revision (`supersededByRevision: "B"`). The Drawing sheets tab displays an expandable "Drawing revisions & history" control with `CURRENT` and `SUPERSEDED` status badges and an issue register table. Clicking "Inspect layout" on an older revision retrieves the frozen layout onto the canvas stage, with a prominent `.arch-superseded-banner` alert and a diagonal semi-transparent red `SUPERSEDED` SVG watermark across the paper drawing, while locking viewport and sheet editing controls. Proven by 8 unit tests covering issue recording, stale-review refusal, supersession transitions, retrievability of modified/deleted sheets, and chronological lineage (92/92 architect tests passing, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0), plus an inspected Fast CDP browser scenario (`proof/growth/2026-09-12-d09-revisions/README.md`, `fast-cdp-execution.log`, 3 screenshots at 1680×1050). Remaining, and why this is not verified: development browser only, with no production minification build, no installed desktop package run, and no tablet capture; revision lineage is single-sequence rather than multi-party branching; and historical issues are persisted in client project state / LocalStorage rather than a central cloud-synced revision vault.
