+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:160](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L160) — **D-13 Batch printing and issue sets** — Selected sheets export in reviewed order with an issue register. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-12). Implemented: selected sheets are issued as one PDF whose first page is a drawing issue register listing every sheet in printed order with its number, size, scale and viewport count, plus the issue purpose, design revision, model revision and timestamp. Order follows the design's managed sheet order rather than click order, so the issued set matches the register the user reads on screen. An issue is reviewed before export and the review is refused if the design changed after it, in the UI and again inside the export function so a programmatic caller cannot bypass it. Each sheet renders through the existing single-sheet path and the pages are merged, so an issued drawing is the drawing the user saw, and mixed A1/A3 paper sizes survive (`src/studio/architect/issueSet.ts`, `sheets.ts` exportIssueSetPdf, `ArchitectSheets.tsx`). Proven by reading a committed 5-page issue back from its own bytes and by an inspected desktop browser journey covering selection, review and the stale-review refusal; 73/73 tests, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0 (proof/growth/2026-09-12-d13-issue-set/README.md). Remaining, and why this is not verified: development-server browser only, with no built-browser or installed-app run and no tablet capture; the browser proof does not exercise the file download itself; and no issue history is stored, so the project holds no record of what was issued when, which D-09 supersession would need. Single-sheet PDF export remains assessed under D-08.
