+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:162](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L162) — **D-15 Visual and vector revision delta** — Two issued revisions report added, removed and changed geometry with a quantity variance table. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-12). Implemented: pure revision delta comparison engine (`src/studio/architect/revisionDelta.ts`) and project geometry snapshot capture on drawing issue (`src/studio/architect/issueHistory.ts`, `model.ts`). When an issue set is exported, a frozen geometry snapshot of project levels, walls, hosted openings, slabs, roofs, and annotations is saved alongside the sheet layouts. In the Drawing sheets tab (`src/studio/architect/ArchitectSheets.tsx`), an interactive "Compare revisions (Revision Delta)" panel enables instant comparison between any two issued revisions (e.g. Rev A vs Rev B) or between an issue and live WIP design. Reports: (1) high-level KPI cards for sheet modifications, geometry changes, net area variance, and material cost delta; (2) color-coded delta cards for added, removed, and modified sheets (detecting size, scale, and layout hash differences); (3) vector geometry element delta cards tracking modified wall lengths/alignments/layers, hosted door/window parameters (sill, hinge, swing, dimensions), slabs, and roofs; and (4) an interactive Quantity Variance Schedule with trade/material breakdowns, unit of measurement, baseline vs target quantities, delta (Δ) with color-coded badges, and percentage change. Proven by 7 unit tests (99/99 architect tests passing, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0) and an inspected Fast CDP browser scenario (`proof/growth/2026-09-12-d15-delta/README.md`, `fast-cdp-execution.log`, 3 screenshots at 1680×1050). Remaining, and why this is not verified: development browser only, with no production minification build, no installed desktop package run, and no tablet capture; geometry delta uses element ID and parameter diffing rather than raster pixel-diff shaders or 3D mesh boolean intersection; and historical issues and snapshots are persisted in client project state / LocalStorage rather than a central cloud-synced revision vault. Review corrections 2026-09-12: legacy geometry now fails closed, missed element/layout changes are detected, and slab/roof detail cards are complete. Machine tests pass; full interaction proof remains pending. Prior annotation-comparison and legacy-fallback claims are superseded by proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md. Review corrections 2026-09-12: legacy geometry now fails closed, missed element/layout changes are detected, and slab/roof detail cards are complete. Machine tests pass; full interaction proof remains pending. Prior annotation-comparison and legacy-fallback claims are superseded by proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:454](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L454) — **T-01 Scale calibration per sheet** — Known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Per-sheet calibration converts every supported input unit to metres, round-trips points through a rotated, scaled and translated transform, and is stored per page with duplicate page records rejected and version-1 records migrated (`src/studio/calibration.ts`; `calibration.test.ts`). Remaining: measurement after a deliberate sheet rotation and reload is asserted at transform level, not through an inspected UI journey.
