 ### C — CAD precision and drawing tools
 
 Benchmark references: [Autodesk AutoCAD](https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad). These references inform the category; each acceptance requirement is X-Ray's own target.
 
-- [ ] **C-01 Lines, polylines, arcs and circles** — Exact coordinates survive save and CAD exchange. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Lines, arcs and circles are authored entities and survive a hash-bound DXF round trip that restores stable IDs exactly (`src/studio/architect/model.ts`, `exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts` "DXF parametric round trip preserves stable IDs"). A general open polyline entity does not exist: an imported LWPOLYLINE is exploded into separate lines. Remaining: a polyline entity, and coordinate survival through DWG and IFC rather than DXF alone.
-- [ ] **C-02 Splines and curves** — Control points and curve tolerance survive supported exchanges. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No spline or NURBS entity exists in the model schema. Curved geometry is limited to circles and arcs. There is nothing to assess until a curve type is authored.
-- [ ] **C-03 Object snaps and tracking** — Endpoint, midpoint, perpendicular and intersection picks are correct. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Seven snap kinds are computed geometrically and each is asserted independently, including line-circle and circle-circle intersections and a tangent at an irrational point (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts` snapPoint; `architect.test.ts` "snap candidates resolve endpoint, midpoint, intersection, perpendicular, extension, centre and tangent"; 72 tests logged 2026-09-10). Remaining: no inspected screenshot of live cursor snapping at the declared viewports, so the row stays partial under the tick rule.
-- [ ] **C-04 Numeric and relative entry** — Typed distance/angle yields the expected measured geometry. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Typed length with ortho and polar angle stepping resolves to the exact constrained distance (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts` constrainPoint, asserted at 4500 mm on a 30 degree polar step). Remaining: typed angle and absolute or relative coordinate entry are not implemented, and there is no visual proof.
-- [ ] **C-05 Coordinate systems and origins** — Local and project origins transform without drift. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). A single global millimetre space with level elevations is implemented. There is no user coordinate system, origin relocation or rotated working plane, so the row cannot be assessed.
-- [ ] **C-06 Layers and visibility** — Hidden, locked and isolated layers retain correct entity membership. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No CAD drafting layer exists. The model field named layers is a wall assembly material layer, not a visibility or lock container, and DXF export synthesises layer names from levels. Recorded explicitly because the field name invites a false positive.
-- [ ] **C-07 Selection and properties** — Window/crossing selection and batch edits affect intended objects only. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Selection is a single entity id. Window and crossing selection, multi-select and batch property edits are not implemented.
-- [ ] **C-08 Move, rotate, scale and copy** — Transform and undo preserve dimensions and IDs. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Move, rotate, scale, copy and array are not implemented as transforms. Offset and mirror each derive one copy, which does not satisfy this row.
-- [ ] **C-09 Offset, trim, extend and fillet** — Edge cases retain valid connected geometry. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Offset, mirror, trim, extend and a tangential fillet are real solvers with asserted results and explicit edge-case refusals: a radius too large for its segments, parallel segments that cannot meet, and an intersection already inside the segment are each rejected with a stated reason (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts`; `architect.test.ts` "precision exact length, mirror, offset, trim, extend and tangential fillet"). Remaining: no inspected screenshot, and connected-geometry survival is proven per operation rather than across a drawing session.
-- [ ] **C-10 Blocks and reusable symbols** — Definition update changes intended instances without broken attributes. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No block, symbol or instance definition exists.
-- [ ] **C-11 Constraints and parameters** — Driving dimension regenerates dependent geometry consistently. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No geometric or dimensional constraint solver exists. Wall-hosted dimensions report geometry; they do not drive it.
-- [ ] **C-12 Dimensions, leaders and text** — Annotation values update and plot legibly at scale. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Wall-hosted dimensions are associative: moving a wall end from 4000 to 5000 mm regenerates the annotation text, and plan, elevation and section views regenerate with it (`src/studio/architect/drawing.ts`; `architect.test.ts` "plan, elevations, sections and associative dimensions regenerate after editing"). Remaining: free-standing linear, aligned, angular and radial dimensions, leaders and user-placed text do not exist, and plotted legibility at scale is unproven.
