 ### E — Estimation, pricing and commercial work
 
 Benchmark references: [RIB CostX](https://www.rib-software.com/en/rib-costx), [One Click LCA life-cycle costing](https://oneclicklca.com/en-gb/software/design-construction/life-cycle-costing). These references inform the category; each acceptance requirement is X-Ray's own target.
 
-- [ ] **E-01 Pricing workbook import** — XLSX/CSV sheets preview without executing spreadsheet formulas. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for bounded XLSX and CSV preview with no spreadsheet formula execution: a mapped formula is refused despite a cached value, malformed input is preserved, and reload passes in the declared browser and Windows scenarios (`src/studio/priceWorkbook.ts`). Remaining: a 2 MiB source and 20 MiB expanded archive limit, no XLS, XLSM or encrypted files, and the rates used were QA fixtures rather than supplier quotations.
-- [ ] **E-02 Column and worksheet mapping** — SKU, description, unit and rate map with row-level errors. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for worksheet and heading selection and SKU, description, unit and rate mapping with row and cell errors, where explicit review precedes saving and the source hash, selected worksheet and physical rows survive reload (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: no inferred currency or unit conversion, and the original workbook bytes are not embedded in backups.
-- [ ] **E-03 Named price books and revisions** — Supplier revisions coexist and old estimates remain reproducible. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Price books are append-only and revisioned so supplier revisions coexist and an earlier revision remains readable, with archive supported and a live CSV import creating a named book at library revision 1 (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`; SC-12 journey). Remaining: reproducing an old estimate against its original revision has not been executed.
-- [ ] **E-04 Currency, tax and effective dates** — Mixed currencies never total without a reviewed conversion. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Currency is ISO-4217 validated and totals are grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places and summed in integer minor units, so mixed currencies never silently total, and an effective date and tax basis are carried per book (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: there is no reviewed conversion path, so mixed currencies are separated rather than converted.
-- [ ] **E-05 Unit and pack normalization** — Each/metre/square-metre/pack conversion shows its dimensional basis. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Unit is free text carried through from the source workbook. There is no unit or pack normalisation and no dimensional basis display, so the row cannot be assessed.
-- [ ] **E-06 Apply and remove a price book** — Impact preview preserves manual overrides and supports undo. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). A price book cannot be applied to measured quantities or removed from them. Worksheet lines can be priced individually, and the quantity bridge returns an explicit unavailable status (`src/studio/crmBridge.ts`).
-- [ ] **E-07 Supplier quote comparison** — Equal specifications compare landed cost and exclusions. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Supplier quote comparison with landed cost and exclusions is not implemented.
-- [ ] **E-08 Material, labour and plant build-ups** — Assembly rate reconciles to separately editable components. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-19; SC-10 proof updated 2026-09-20). QS contractor revisions independently pin material and labour supplier revisions/lines, or record explicit labour exclusion; waste, markup and tax remain separate. Domain tests and the DANS1 measured-run UI reconcile AUD55 material +10 labour +13 markup +7.80 GST =85.80 for the controlled 5m base row. [Original partial evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-19-sc10-qs-rate-delta/AZ-PARTIAL-ASSESSMENT.md); [current exact-decimal workflow, tests, screenshots and diff](proof/growth/2026-09-20-sc10-use-measured/steps/SC10-USE-MEASURED-01.md), 297/297 development-browser PASS. Remaining: plant and broader assemblies, production-built/native qualification. Catalogue state remains partial; no row tick or count promotion.
