 ### Q — Quality, checking, compliance and proof
 
 Benchmark references: [buildingSMART IDS](https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/information-delivery-specification-ids/), [CSI ETABS](https://www.csiamerica.com/products/etabs), [Bluebeam markups and data](https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/). These references inform the category; each acceptance requirement is X-Ray's own target.
 
-- [ ] **Q-01 Requirement-to-evidence traceability** — Each acceptance item points to exact fixture and output. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every assessed row in this register names its code path and its executed test or inspected evidence, and slice records carry commands, results, screenshot paths and fixture digests (walkthrough.md; proof/growth/). Remaining: traceability is maintained by discipline in Markdown rather than enforced by a tool that fails when a row loses its evidence.
-- [ ] **Q-02 Smoke tests per delivered change** — Actual screen renders with no uncaught runtime failures. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every delivered slice runs browser journeys that fail on any uncaught page error, and 1,111 tests across 88 suites with a clean typecheck passed on 2026-09-10. Remaining: smoke coverage is per slice rather than a standing gate over every screen.
-- [ ] **Q-03 Screenshot and code-diff proof** — Completed UI row has inspected PNG plus matching source diff. State: verified (assessed 2026-09-10). Enforced by harness rather than convention: the repository guardrail hook blocks a completion claim carrying no proof path, and every accepted row in this register cites a code diff plus an executed log or inspected screenshot (`scripts/guardrails/hook.mjs`, `.claude/settings.json`; proof/growth/2026-09-09-guardrails/pipe-tests.log). Reviewed 2026-09-10.
-- [ ] **Q-04 Model geometry validation** — Invalid solids, overlaps and missing faces are detected and explained. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Geometry validation rejects invalid solids and explains why: overlapping hosted openings, duplicate physical identity, a fillet radius too large for its segments, and cyclic clipping rings from overlapping return walls are each refused with a stated reason (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`, `precision.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: no general missing-face or manifold check across an imported model.
-- [ ] **Q-05 Information requirement checking** — Missing required properties fail the selected rule set. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no information-requirement rule set, so missing properties cannot fail a selected standard.
-- [ ] **Q-06 Clash and clearance checking** — Known hard and clearance clashes are detected without duplicates. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no clash or clearance checking.
-- [ ] **Q-07 Drawing/model/quantity consistency** — Edit updates all linked outputs or marks them stale. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Edits mark dependent outputs stale rather than silently diverging: quantity results are re-verified against their operands and job revision, design material sync invalidates a changed review and retires deleted rows, and dimensions and derived views regenerate from the model (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`, `src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`). Remaining: sheets and exported documents are not linked to the model revision they were produced from.
-- [ ] **Q-08 Engineering benchmark validation** — Independent known cases verify results and supported range. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no engineering solver, so there are no results to validate against independent known cases. Recorded with the S category.
-- [ ] **Q-09 Jurisdiction and edition register** — Every compliance claim identifies applicable published criteria. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No compliance claim is made anywhere in the product, and no jurisdiction or edition register exists. This row stays a gap deliberately rather than being satisfied by silence.
-- [ ] **Q-10 Review and professional sign-off** — Checker identity and limitations remain attached to issued result. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Takeoff evidence is approved for a named person with the approval stamped on the record, and an approval is invalidated when its underlying evidence changes (`src/studio/assistant/takeoffTools.ts`; SC-12 approved a traced run for a named reviewer). Remaining: there is no professional sign-off carrying declared limitations onto an issued output, and without accounts the checker identity is unauthenticated.
-- [ ] **Q-11 Evidence integrity and reproducibility** — Hashes bind source, app build, fixture and result. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Evidence is hash-bound end to end: release stages record frozen source, executable and installer digests, fixtures are hashed, and BOM evidence digests are cross-validated (LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md; proof/growth/2026-09-09-az5-release/). Remaining: reproducing a build from its recorded hashes has not been executed.
-- [ ] **Q-12 Regression and adversarial tests** — Malformed files, cancellations and stale edits preserve data. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Adversarial regressions are executed rather than described: an unsupported schema preserves the original bytes, stale writers are refused, cancelled requests discard late responses, a tampered DXF refuses stale restore, and spreadsheet formulas are never executed on import (`src/studio/persistence.test.ts`, `architect.test.ts`, `src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: coverage is per slice rather than a standing adversarial suite over every store.
-- [ ] **Q-13 Release and installed-app verification** — Installed binary and packaged resources match tested build. State: failed (assessed 2026-09-10). Not achieved and not achievable in the current process: every verified build runs from an isolated profile and the normal installed application has never been replaced, and an earlier installation attempt stalled on a running process that would not close. Recorded as failed rather than open because the release pipeline currently has no installed-app verification step at all (LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md; DWG-TODO.md).
