 ### T — Takeoff, measurement and quantities
 
 Benchmark references: [RIB CostX](https://www.rib-software.com/en/rib-costx), [Bluebeam markups and data](https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/), [Trimble Business Center](https://civilconstruction.trimble.com/en/products/software/trimble-business-center). These references inform the category; each acceptance requirement is X-Ray's own target.
 
-- [ ] **T-01 Scale calibration per sheet** — Known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Per-sheet calibration converts every supported input unit to metres, round-trips points through a rotated, scaled and translated transform, and is stored per page with duplicate page records rejected and version-1 records migrated (`src/studio/calibration.ts`; `calibration.test.ts`). Remaining: measurement after a deliberate sheet rotation and reload is asserted at transform level, not through an inspected UI journey.
-- [ ] **T-02 Separate axes and distorted scans** — Calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Calibration refuses zero-length points, singular transforms and inconsistent converted distances, and records declared, inferred and manual provenance with conflict detection that is independent of candidate order and requires explicit resolution (`src/studio/calibration.ts` reconcileCalibrationCandidates). Remaining: anisotropic separately scaled axes are not represented, so distorted scans are refused rather than measured.
-- [ ] **T-03 Lengths, perimeters and counts** — Totals match independently measured fixture values. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Length, area, count and sketch measurements exist with tracing runs, gates and topology validation (`src/studio/tracing.ts`, `src/studio/store.ts`; tracing suites pass 2026-09-10). The SC-12 journey traced a run at 5.000 m against a locked 5 m calibration. Remaining: totals are not reconciled against an independently measured fixture across a whole sheet set.
-- [ ] **T-04 Areas, holes and net deductions** — Openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Area measurement subtracts openings through real polygon boolean geometry, and the architect model proves an opening removes exact material volume once, a T intersection is a union rather than a sum, and overlapping or duplicate hosted openings are rejected (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: net deduction is proven in the design model, not for user-drawn takeoff polygons with holes on a source sheet.
-- [ ] **T-05 Volumes, slopes and elevations** — 3D quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Volume carries an explicit basis: the area-depth method names its calibration and every depth evidence id, and results are re-verified against their operands and job revision so a stale snapshot is refused (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`). Remaining: projected versus actual sloped surface area is not distinguished, which is the substance of this row.
-- [ ] **T-06 Trade and work-package classification** — Reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Quantities group by trade only. There is no work-package or standard classification such as NRM, Uniclass or CSI, and therefore no reclassification behaviour to assess.
-- [ ] **T-07 Assembly breakdowns** — Element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Element quantities decompose into material rows with declared density, rate revision and waste, and design material sync is idempotent, preserves physical rows, invalidates a changed review and retires deletions (`src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: assumptions are recorded per material rather than presented as a reviewable assembly breakdown.
-- [ ] **T-08 Duplicate detection and exclusions** — Overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Overlapping takeoffs are not detected or presented for review before totalling.
-- [ ] **T-09 Revision quantity comparison** — Additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision comparison that reconciles additions, removals and changed quantities against a prior issue.
-- [ ] **T-10 Measurement source links** — Each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every calculation operand requires at least one evidence reference, and document, calibration and photo evidence identity and digests are cross-validated (`src/studio/bomContract.ts`; BOM suites pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: opening the exact page region from a quantity is not proven by an inspected journey.
-- [ ] **T-11 Stock lengths, packs and wastage** — Purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Waste is applied as a percentage that produces an order quantity distinct from net measured demand on architect wall layers (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts` quantity and cost use net geometry, explicit density, rate revision and waste). Remaining: stock lengths and pack sizes are not modelled, and waste is unavailable on source-sheet takeoff markups.
-- [ ] **T-12 Manual, model and AI quantity provenance** — User can distinguish and review each quantity origin. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provenance is enforced rather than optional: calibration candidates carry method, evidence and document id, and a candidate with empty evidence is rejected by test. Assistant-created measurements carry tool receipts bound to a revision (SC-12). Remaining: manual, model and AI origins are not surfaced as a single reviewable distinction in the interface.
-- [ ] **T-13 Reconciliation and audit exports** — Summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Money totals are summed in integer minor units grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places, so summary figures reproduce their rows without floating-point drift, and CSV export escapes formula-leading cells (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: a reconciliation export that reproduces detailed rows with units and declared rounding is not implemented.
-- [ ] **T-14 Bulk edit, undo and recovery** — Batch operation restores all affected quantities and associations. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch edit over quantities, and therefore no batch undo or recovery of affected associations.
-- [ ] **T-15 Cost code and classification binding** — Every measured item maps to a user-definable classification hierarchy and reports with no unclassified residue. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). Added to the register on 2026-09-11 from the quantity surveying specification. T-06 trade and work-package classification is a gap and covers trade grouping; this row covers binding to an extensible cost-code hierarchy so an estimate can be reported, benchmarked and compared between revisions. Without it the whole quantity surveying profile is blocked at its second task. Source: planning/PROPOSED-REGISTER-EXPANSIONS.md.
