 ### V — Versioning, collaboration and staff handoff
 
 Benchmark references: [Graphisoft BIMcloud teams](https://helpcenter.graphisoft.com/user-guide/134439/), [buildingSMART BCF](https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/bim-collaboration-format/), [Oracle Aconex](https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/), [Autodesk Forma construction document management](https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/). These references inform the category; each acceptance requirement is X-Ray's own target.
 
-- [ ] **V-01 Named project versions** — Saved milestone reopens exact drawing, sources and commercial state. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Project and design revisions increment only on a real structural change, a no-op keeps the revision, and stale writes are refused against the last loaded bytes (`src/studio/architect/model.ts` revise; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: there is no browsable version history to restore from.
-- [ ] **V-02 Change comparisons** — Reviewer can inspect changed objects, quantities, documents and rates. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no change comparison across objects, quantities, documents and rates.
-- [ ] **V-03 Staff handoff package** — Fresh recipient profile restores complete reviewed project context. State: partial (reviewed 2026-09-11). A transferred v2 package now restores source-linked saved work into a fresh isolated browser context, with a recovery copy and protected original insertion. Code: src/studio/workspaceRestoreStorage.ts. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-restore/README.md. Remaining: full reviewed-context fixture coverage, explicitly excluded assistant/runtime context and actual named-recipient acceptance; no external delivery was performed.
-- [ ] **V-04 Selective package content** — Private rates and unrelated documents are excluded by review. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Package content cannot be selected or reviewed for exclusion, so private rates cannot be withheld.
-- [ ] **V-05 Recipient and distribution list** — Intended staff and access level are visible before sending. State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). The external handoff bridge returns an explicit unavailable result by design and no recipient or access level can be chosen (`src/studio/crmBridge.ts`). Blocked on an account service and an authenticated transport.
-- [ ] **V-06 Transmittals and receipts** — Sent status requires durable receipt rather than button click. State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Nothing is sent, so no durable receipt exists. The bridge reports unavailable rather than implying delivery, which is the honest state but not a pass.
-- [ ] **V-07 Download links and expiry** — Revoked or expired link cannot fetch protected documents. State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no download links, expiry or revocation.
-- [ ] **V-08 Assignments and notifications** — Task owner receives only relevant authorized information. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Assignments and notifications are not implemented.
-- [ ] **V-09 Comments and review decisions** — Replies retain authorship and referenced revision. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Comments and review decisions are not implemented.
-- [ ] **V-10 Checkout/reservation and live collaboration** — Concurrent edits resolve without silent last-writer loss. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Concurrent editing is handled by refusal rather than merging: a stale writer is blocked, another window marks the workspace stale and pauses silent autosave, and a reload recovers the newer revision (`src/studio/store.ts`, `persistence.ts`; SC-02). Remaining: there is no checkout, reservation or live collaboration, and the native two-window case is not drivable through the test harness.
-- [ ] **V-11 Merge and conflict review** — Both versions remain recoverable until explicit resolution. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no merge or conflict review. A refused stale write preserves the stored copy but discards nothing of the rejected edit into a recoverable form.
-- [ ] **V-12 Approval stages and issued status** — Work-in-progress cannot appear as approved construction issue. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no approval stages or issued status, so work in progress cannot be distinguished from a construction issue.
