 ### X — Extensibility, automation and AI assistance
 
 Benchmark references: [Firecrawl v2 search API](https://docs.firecrawl.dev/api-reference/endpoint/search), [buildingSMART IDS](https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/information-delivery-specification-ids/), [AVEVA Unified Engineering](https://www.aveva.com/en/products/unified-engineering/). These references inform the category; each acceptance requirement is X-Ray's own target.
 
-- [ ] **X-01 Plugin and adapter boundaries** — Extension failure cannot corrupt the project store. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no plugin or adapter boundary, so extension isolation cannot be assessed. The nearest boundary is the native CAD engine subprocess, which is a bundled component rather than a third-party extension.
-- [ ] **X-02 Versioned data schema** — Unsupported schema is rejected with original bytes preserved. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unsupported project schema version fails closed with a stated expected version and returns the original stored bytes untouched, while a supported legacy version migrates forward, both asserted by test (`src/studio/persistence.ts`; `persistence.test.ts` fails closed for an unknown schema version). The architect store separately proves a future schema cannot be bypassed by ordinary edits. Remaining: no inspected screenshot of the user-facing refusal.
-- [ ] **X-03 Custom workflows and forms** — Organization can add fields and stages without source-code edits. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Custom workflows and forms cannot be defined without source changes.
-- [ ] **X-04 Rules and calculation extensions** — Execution is bounded and results identify rule version. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no user-supplied rule or calculation extension, so bounded execution and rule versioning cannot be assessed.
-- [ ] **X-05 Batch processing queue** — Jobs are resumable, cancellable and individually diagnosed. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch processing queue with resumable, cancellable, individually diagnosed jobs. Individual long operations are assessed under U-08.
-- [ ] **X-06 AI extraction from source plans** — Suggested object retains exact source region and uncertainty. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). AI proposals are validated before they touch the design, with bounds, room closure and hosted-door checks and review-time revision binding, so a proposal built against an older revision is refused (`src/studio/architect/layoutAi.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: extraction from a source plan does not retain an exact source region or an uncertainty value, which is the substance of this row.
-- [ ] **X-07 AI layout/design proposals** — Proposal is separately reviewable before modifying authored design. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Proposals cannot silently modify the authored design: validation runs first, the permission mode governs whether an edit executes, and a refusal is returned to the model as a tool error it can read (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`, `useAssistantChat.ts`; permission suite passes 2026-09-10). Remaining: no side-by-side proposal preview before acceptance.
-- [ ] **X-08 Voice and natural-language actions** — Intended edit is understandable and reversible. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Natural-language actions map to real tools with plain-word intents that never expose raw JSON, and every design edit is undoable through the same history as a manual edit; live journeys drew, edited and undid geometry by entity identifier (SC-08, SC-12, SC-15). Remaining: voice input does not conduct an autonomous conversation.
-- [ ] **X-09 AI pricing research assistant** — Source evidence accompanies suggested supplier match and rate. State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). The assistant can read price books and import a pasted price book with recorded provenance, but it cannot research a supplier rate because the search credential is not configured and no application path exists (P-03, P-08). Blocked on the same dependency.
-- [ ] **X-10 Tool permission and secret boundaries** — AI cannot reveal keys or issue unapproved external mutations. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provider keys are read only inside server modules under `src/lib/*.server.ts` and never reach browser code, and unapproved external mutation is blocked by the permission gate: in ask mode no edit tool runs until the user allows it, and a stop denies the pending prompt (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`, 36 tests pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: no adversarial attempt to extract a key through the model has been executed.
-- [ ] **X-11 Usage limits and cost reporting** — Provider usage is capped and reported per operation. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Usage is estimated and reported as a context meter with a hard stop at the declared budget, folding in provider caps on entries, images and request bytes (`src/studio/assistant/contextBudget.ts`). Remaining: per-operation monetary cost is not reported, and the estimate is a client-side approximation rather than provider-reported usage.
-- [ ] **X-12 Human review and rejection** — Rejected proposal leaves authoritative design unchanged. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A denied permission prompt leaves the design unchanged and returns an explicit refusal rather than failing silently, asserted across allow once, allow for this chat, deny and stop (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`). Remaining: rejecting an already-applied change relies on undo rather than a proposal queue.
-- [ ] **X-13 Automation provenance** — Prompt/input version, tool and accepted changes are traceable. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Work packets persist the objective, the actions taken and the raw task events, and tool receipts are bound to the design revision they changed (`src/studio/assistant/workPacket.ts`, `workPacketStore.ts`). Remaining: the prompt or manual version in force is not recorded alongside the accepted changes.
-- [ ] **X-14 Integration health and retries** — Unavailable service is visible and retry does not duplicate work. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unconfigured or failing provider is reported truthfully rather than hidden: the pricing route distinguishes not-configured, 401, 402, 429, timeout, abort, oversized and malformed responses, and single-flight refusal prevents a duplicate in-flight request (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: there is no automatic retry policy, so retry without duplication is proven only for the refusal path.
