_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a> · <a href="https://civilconstruction.trimble.com/en/products/software/trimble-business-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trimble Business Center</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="t-01 scale calibration per sheet known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-01</div><div><strong>Scale calibration per sheet</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Per-sheet calibration converts every supported input unit to metres, round-trips points through a rotated, scaled and translated transform, and is stored per page with duplicate page records rejected and version-1 records migrated (`src/studio/calibration.ts`; `calibration.test.ts`). Remaining: measurement after a deliberate sheet rotation and reload is asserted at transform level, not through an inspected UI journey.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-02 separate axes and distorted scans calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-02</div><div><strong>Separate axes and distorted scans</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Calibration refuses zero-length points, singular transforms and inconsistent converted distances, and records declared, inferred and manual provenance with conflict detection that is independent of candidate order and requires explicit resolution (`src/studio/calibration.ts` reconcileCalibrationCandidates). Remaining: anisotropic separately scaled axes are not represented, so distorted scans are refused rather than measured.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-03 lengths, perimeters and counts totals match independently measured fixture values"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-03</div><div><strong>Lengths, perimeters and counts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Totals match independently measured fixture values.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Length, area, count and sketch measurements exist with tracing runs, gates and topology validation (`src/studio/tracing.ts`, `src/studio/store.ts`; tracing suites pass 2026-09-10). The SC-12 journey traced a run at 5.000 m against a locked 5 m calibration. Remaining: totals are not reconciled against an independently measured fixture across a whole sheet set.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-04 areas, holes and net deductions openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-04</div><div><strong>Areas, holes and net deductions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Area measurement subtracts openings through real polygon boolean geometry, and the architect model proves an opening removes exact material volume once, a T intersection is a union rather than a sum, and overlapping or duplicate hosted openings are rejected (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: net deduction is proven in the design model, not for user-drawn takeoff polygons with holes on a source sheet.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-05 volumes, slopes and elevations 3d quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-05</div><div><strong>Volumes, slopes and elevations</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: 3D quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Volume carries an explicit basis: the area-depth method names its calibration and every depth evidence id, and results are re-verified against their operands and job revision so a stale snapshot is refused (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`). Remaining: projected versus actual sloped surface area is not distinguished, which is the substance of this row.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-06 trade and work-package classification reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-06</div><div><strong>Trade and work-package classification</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Quantities group by trade only. There is no work-package or standard classification such as NRM, Uniclass or CSI, and therefore no reclassification behaviour to assess.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-07 assembly breakdowns element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-07</div><div><strong>Assembly breakdowns</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Element quantities decompose into material rows with declared density, rate revision and waste, and design material sync is idempotent, preserves physical rows, invalidates a changed review and retires deletions (`src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: assumptions are recorded per material rather than presented as a reviewable assembly breakdown.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-08 duplicate detection and exclusions overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-08</div><div><strong>Duplicate detection and exclusions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Overlapping takeoffs are not detected or presented for review before totalling.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-09 revision quantity comparison additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-09</div><div><strong>Revision quantity comparison</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision comparison that reconciles additions, removals and changed quantities against a prior issue.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-10 measurement source links each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-10</div><div><strong>Measurement source links</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every calculation operand requires at least one evidence reference, and document, calibration and photo evidence identity and digests are cross-validated (`src/studio/bomContract.ts`; BOM suites pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: opening the exact page region from a quantity is not proven by an inspected journey.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-11 stock lengths, packs and wastage purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-11</div><div><strong>Stock lengths, packs and wastage</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Waste is applied as a percentage that produces an order quantity distinct from net measured demand on architect wall layers (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts` quantity and cost use net geometry, explicit density, rate revision and waste). Remaining: stock lengths and pack sizes are not modelled, and waste is unavailable on source-sheet takeoff markups.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-12 manual, model and ai quantity provenance user can distinguish and review each quantity origin"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-12</div><div><strong>Manual, model and AI quantity provenance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: User can distinguish and review each quantity origin.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provenance is enforced rather than optional: calibration candidates carry method, evidence and document id, and a candidate with empty evidence is rejected by test. Assistant-created measurements carry tool receipts bound to a revision (SC-12). Remaining: manual, model and AI origins are not surfaced as a single reviewable distinction in the interface.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-13 reconciliation and audit exports summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-13</div><div><strong>Reconciliation and audit exports</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Money totals are summed in integer minor units grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places, so summary figures reproduce their rows without floating-point drift, and CSV export escapes formula-leading cells (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: a reconciliation export that reproduces detailed rows with units and declared rounding is not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-14 bulk edit, undo and recovery batch operation restores all affected quantities and associations"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-14</div><div><strong>Bulk edit, undo and recovery</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Batch operation restores all affected quantities and associations.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch edit over quantities, and therefore no batch undo or recovery of affected associations.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-15 cost code and classification binding every measured item maps to a user-definable classification hierarchy and reports with no unclassified residue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-15</div><div><strong>Cost code and classification binding</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Every measured item maps to a user-definable classification hierarchy and reports with no unclassified residue.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). Added to the register on 2026-09-11 from the quantity surveying specification. T-06 trade and work-package classification is a gap and covers trade grouping; this row covers binding to an extensible cost-code hierarchy so an estimate can be reported, benchmarked and compared between revisions. Without it the whole quantity surveying profile is blocked at its second task. Source: planning/PROPOSED-REGISTER-EXPANSIONS.md.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-U" data-category="U"><div class="cathead"><h2>U — Usability, performance and everyday flexibility</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a> · <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="u-01 role-specific workspace presets architect and estimator get useful tools without separate data copies"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-01</div><div><strong>Role-specific workspace presets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Architect and estimator get useful tools without separate data copies.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Workspaces separate architect, source, model, sheets, pricing and render surfaces over one shared project record, so no role requires a separate data copy (`src/studio/WorkspaceRails.tsx`). Remaining: there are no role presets, and without accounts a role cannot be selected.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-02 search, command palette and shortcuts common commands work from keyboard and show discoverable labels"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-02</div><div><strong>Search, command palette and shortcuts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Common commands work from keyboard and show discoverable labels.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-03 resizable panels and saved layouts layout restores on the user&#39;s monitor without hiding actions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-03</div><div><strong>Resizable panels and saved layouts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Layout restores on the user&#39;s monitor without hiding actions.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Panels resize and persist: the assistant panel resizes from four corners and can dock into the right rail, the Magic Pencil dock is draggable and clamped back into view on resize, and top menu rows resize with saved layout (`src/studio/assistant/panelCorners.ts`, `draftsmanDockPosition.ts`, `assistantRailMode.ts`; SC-07, SC-14, SC-18). Remaining: layouts are per browser profile and no multi-monitor case is covered.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-04 large plan/model navigation representative heavy fixture meets recorded load and interaction budget"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-04</div><div><strong>Large plan/model navigation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Representative heavy fixture meets recorded load and interaction budget.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Heavy fixtures are exercised in practice: a 13-page source set, a 1,180-part model, a 500 MB attachment path and a 66-wall generated design with 60 windows all load and save (SC-10, SC-17, large-files verification). Remaining: no recorded load and interaction budget exists, so there is no threshold to pass or fail against.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-05 accessible focus, contrast and labels core workflow is usable without pointer or color alone"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-05</div><div><strong>Accessible focus, contrast and labels</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Core workflow is usable without pointer or color alone.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-06 touch and small-screen field use critical actions remain reachable without horizontal clipping"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-06</div><div><strong>Touch and small-screen field use</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Critical actions remain reachable without horizontal clipping.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-07 multi-monitor and high-dpi desktop dialogs and text remain visible at tested scaling levels"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-07</div><div><strong>Multi-monitor and high-DPI desktop</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Dialogs and text remain visible at tested scaling levels.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Multi-monitor and high-DPI scaling have not been tested and no scaling levels are declared.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-08 progress, cancellation and background jobs long operation shows honest status and can be stopped"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-08</div><div><strong>Progress, cancellation and background jobs</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Long operation shows honest status and can be stopped.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Long assistant operations show honest status and can be stopped, with a stop preserving completed tool receipts and denying a pending permission prompt, and provider requests abort and discard late responses (`src/studio/assistant/useAssistantChat.ts`, `src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: import, export and build operations do not report progress or support cancellation uniformly.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-09 useful validation and empty states user can recover from invalid input without losing edits"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-09</div><div><strong>Useful validation and empty states</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: User can recover from invalid input without losing edits.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-10 bulk operations and multi-selection preview clearly reports affected items before applying changes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-10</div><div><strong>Bulk operations and multi-selection</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Preview clearly reports affected items before applying changes.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no multi-selection or bulk operation, so no affected-items preview exists. Related absence is recorded at C-07 and T-14.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-11 per-user preferences and units preference changes do not reinterpret existing geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-11</div><div><strong>Per-user preferences and units</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Preference changes do not reinterpret existing geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Preferences are validated and migrated rather than trusted, and legacy appearance settings migrate while malformed values are refused without corrupting stored settings (appearance and menu preference suites pass 2026-09-10). Units are fixed to millimetres, so a preference change cannot reinterpret geometry. Remaining: there is no per-user unit choice to test against.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-12 localization and terminology industry-specific terms do not change underlying data meaning"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-12</div><div><strong>Localization and terminology</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Industry-specific terms do not change underlying data meaning.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no localisation or terminology mapping.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-13 onboarding and sample isolation sample work cannot be mistaken for the user&#39;s source project"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-13</div><div><strong>Onboarding and sample isolation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Sample work cannot be mistaken for the user&#39;s source project.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Sample and demonstration data are firewalled from verified output: sample sources are flagged, the assistant reports origin and sample status when reading a building, and fixture data is barred from verified price and quote outputs (`src/studio/assistant/workbenchStructure.ts`, `read_source_building` origin and sample fields). Remaining: there is no onboarding flow, and the separation is proven in tool contracts rather than an inspected journey.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-14 support diagnostics and recovery guidance export omits secrets and includes reproducible failure context"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-14</div><div><strong>Support diagnostics and recovery guidance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Export omits secrets and includes reproducible failure context.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no support diagnostic export, so secret omission and reproducible failure context cannot be assessed.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-V" data-category="V"><div class="cathead"><h2>V — Versioning, collaboration and staff handoff</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://helpcenter.graphisoft.com/user-guide/134439/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Graphisoft BIMcloud teams</a> · <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/bim-collaboration-format/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART BCF</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a> · <a href="https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Forma construction document management</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="v-01 named project versions saved milestone reopens exact drawing, sources and commercial state"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-01</div><div><strong>Named project versions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Saved milestone reopens exact drawing, sources and commercial state.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Project and design revisions increment only on a real structural change, a no-op keeps the revision, and stale writes are refused against the last loaded bytes (`src/studio/architect/model.ts` revise; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: there is no browsable version history to restore from.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-02 change comparisons reviewer can inspect changed objects, quantities, documents and rates"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-02</div><div><strong>Change comparisons</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reviewer can inspect changed objects, quantities, documents and rates.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no change comparison across objects, quantities, documents and rates.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-03 staff handoff package fresh recipient profile restores complete reviewed project context"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-03</div><div><strong>Staff handoff package</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Fresh recipient profile restores complete reviewed project context.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (reviewed 2026-09-11). A transferred v2 package now restores source-linked saved work into a fresh isolated browser context, with a recovery copy and protected original insertion. Code: src/studio/workspaceRestoreStorage.ts. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-restore/README.md. Remaining: full reviewed-context fixture coverage, explicitly excluded assistant/runtime context and actual named-recipient acceptance; no external delivery was performed.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-04 selective package content private rates and unrelated documents are excluded by review"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-04</div><div><strong>Selective package content</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Private rates and unrelated documents are excluded by review.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Package content cannot be selected or reviewed for exclusion, so private rates cannot be withheld.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-05 recipient and distribution list intended staff and access level are visible before sending"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-05</div><div><strong>Recipient and distribution list</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Intended staff and access level are visible before sending.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). The external handoff bridge returns an explicit unavailable result by design and no recipient or access level can be chosen (`src/studio/crmBridge.ts`). Blocked on an account service and an authenticated transport.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-06 transmittals and receipts sent status requires durable receipt rather than button click"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-06</div><div><strong>Transmittals and receipts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Sent status requires durable receipt rather than button click.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Nothing is sent, so no durable receipt exists. The bridge reports unavailable rather than implying delivery, which is the honest state but not a pass.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-07 download links and expiry revoked or expired link cannot fetch protected documents"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-07</div><div><strong>Download links and expiry</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Revoked or expired link cannot fetch protected documents.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no download links, expiry or revocation.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-08 assignments and notifications task owner receives only relevant authorized information"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-08</div><div><strong>Assignments and notifications</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Task owner receives only relevant authorized information.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Assignments and notifications are not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-09 comments and review decisions replies retain authorship and referenced revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-09</div><div><strong>Comments and review decisions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Replies retain authorship and referenced revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Comments and review decisions are not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-10 checkout/reservation and live collaboration concurrent edits resolve without silent last-writer loss"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-10</div><div><strong>Checkout/reservation and live collaboration</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Concurrent edits resolve without silent last-writer loss.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Concurrent editing is handled by refusal rather than merging: a stale writer is blocked, another window marks the workspace stale and pauses silent autosave, and a reload recovers the newer revision (`src/studio/store.ts`, `persistence.ts`; SC-02). Remaining: there is no checkout, reservation or live collaboration, and the native two-window case is not drivable through the test harness.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-11 merge and conflict review both versions remain recoverable until explicit resolution"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-11</div><div><strong>Merge and conflict review</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Both versions remain recoverable until explicit resolution.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no merge or conflict review. A refused stale write preserves the stored copy but discards nothing of the rejected edit into a recoverable form.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-12 approval stages and issued status work-in-progress cannot appear as approved construction issue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-12</div><div><strong>Approval stages and issued status</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Work-in-progress cannot appear as approved construction issue.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no approval stages or issued status, so work in progress cannot be distinguished from a construction issue.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-13 external consultant exchanges returned package reconciles identity and reported differences"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-13</div><div><strong>External consultant exchanges</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Returned package reconciles identity and reported differences.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). External consultant exchange and reconciliation are not implemented.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="v-14 organization boundaries and activity logs cross-company sharing exposes only authorized content"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>V-14</div><div><strong>Organization boundaries and activity logs</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Cross-company sharing exposes only authorized content.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There are no organisation boundaries or activity logs.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-W" data-category="W"><div class="cathead"><h2>W — Whole-life performance, sustainability and risk</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.iesve.com/software/virtual-environment" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IES Virtual Environment</a> · <a href="https://oneclicklca.com/en-be/software/design-construction" target="_blank" rel="noopene