equirement" data-search="y-12 agricultural and rural infrastructure fencing, sheds, irrigation and access reconcile site records"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Y-12</div><div><strong>Agricultural and rural infrastructure</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Fencing, sheds, irrigation and access reconcile site records.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No yards, infrastructure or industrial-asset module exists. These specialist asset types have no representation in the data model. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="y-13 temporary events and modular facilities reusable configuration retains load and installation reviews"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Y-13</div><div><strong>Temporary events and modular facilities</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reusable configuration retains load and installation reviews.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No yards, infrastructure or industrial-asset module exists. These specialist asset types have no representation in the data model. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="y-14 brownfield retrofit and decommissioning existing/removed/new assets stay distinct with source evidence"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Y-14</div><div><strong>Brownfield retrofit and decommissioning</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Existing/removed/new assets stay distinct with source evidence.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No yards, infrastructure or industrial-asset module exists. These specialist asset types have no representation in the data model. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-Z" data-category="Z"><div class="cathead"><h2>Z — Zero-loss delivery, release and business continuity</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Forma construction document management</a> · <a href="https://www.ibm.com/products/maximo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">IBM Maximo</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="z-01 reproducible build identity proof records commit, dirty diff and artifact hashes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-01</div><div><strong>Reproducible build identity</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Proof records commit, dirty diff and artifact hashes.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Release stages freeze the source, count the collected files, record executable and installer digests, inject and verify a build identity and check for source drift after quality assurance (proof/growth/2026-09-09-az5-release/verification.md; LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md). Remaining: builds run from an uncommitted working tree, so a commit and dirty-diff record is not part of the identity.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-02 desktop install and upgrade upgrade retains real user profile and compatible project data"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-02</div><div><strong>Desktop install and upgrade</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Upgrade retains real user profile and compatible project data.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No build has been installed over the normal application. Every verified package runs from an isolated profile and the register must not imply an upgrade path was tested.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-03 offline cold start installed app opens source and design without development services"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-03</div><div><strong>Offline cold start</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Installed app opens source and design without development services.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). The packaged Windows application starts and completes journeys from an isolated profile without development services, including retained sheets, price books and saved views (SC-11, SC-13 native runs). Remaining: cold start is proven for the packaged executable, not for an installed application.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-04 web production parity built site completes the same declared workflows as development"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-04</div><div><strong>Web production parity</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Built site completes the same declared workflows as development.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Each release runs the same declared journeys against the built site and the native application, most recently 40 runs and 765 commands across both for build 8e14ac427997. Remaining: parity is asserted for the declared journeys only, with rendering web-only and the native refusal documented.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-05 dependency and license inventory bundled components carry required notices and versions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-05</div><div><strong>Dependency and license inventory</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Bundled components carry required notices and versions.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no dependency and licence inventory with required notices. A bundled third-party CAD engine and a CC0 asset are recorded individually in their slices, which does not satisfy this row.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-06 security and tenant isolation adversarial access tests cannot cross project permissions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-06</div><div><strong>Security and tenant isolation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Adversarial access tests cannot cross project permissions.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no tenants or permissions to cross. Provider keys are confined to server modules (X-10), but adversarial access testing has no boundary to attack until accounts exist.</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-07 backup/restore disaster drill clean machine restoration proves complete recoverability"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-07</div><div><strong>Backup/restore disaster drill</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Clean machine restoration proves complete recoverability.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (reviewed 2026-09-11). The previously missing apply path now restores transferred backup data into fresh browser storage and verifies the original source SHA-256. Code: src/studio/workspaceRestoreStorage.ts. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-restore/README.md. Remaining: clean-machine and native disaster drills with complete project context; a fresh browser context is not a clean machine.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-08 observability without secrets error reports omit keys, private prompts and unauthorized documents"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-08</div><div><strong>Observability without secrets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Error reports omit keys, private prompts and unauthorized documents.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Keys are read only in server modules and never appear in responses, failures or browser code, and evidence bundles are reviewed before archiving (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: there is no error reporting pipeline to audit for private prompts or unauthorised documents.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-09 performance and resource limits oversized files fail safely without freezing or partial writes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-09</div><div><strong>Performance and resource limits</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Oversized files fail safely without freezing or partial writes.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Oversized and malformed inputs fail safely rather than corrupting state: workbook import is bounded against zip expansion, backup capture is capped, the CAD bridge enforces a size limit with cancellation, and a failed write preserves the previously stored bytes. Remaining: no freeze or partial-write behaviour has been measured under a deliberate resource-exhaustion test.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-10 rollback and forward compatibility failed upgrade can recover last confirmed data revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-10</div><div><strong>Rollback and forward compatibility</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Failed upgrade can recover last confirmed data revision.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A newer stored revision is never silently overwritten and an unsupported schema fails closed with the original bytes intact, so the last confirmed data revision survives a refused change (`src/studio/persistence.ts`, `store.ts`). Remaining: there is no application upgrade path, so upgrade rollback is untested.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-11 support and incident handling reproducible ticket links diagnostics, affected build and recovery"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-11</div><div><strong>Support and incident handling</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reproducible ticket links diagnostics, affected build and recovery.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no incident or ticket handling linking diagnostics to an affected build.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-12 proof expiry after changes dependency changes reopen affected completed acceptance rows"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-12</div><div><strong>Proof expiry after changes</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Dependency changes reopen affected completed acceptance rows.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (assessed 2026-09-10). Stated as a governing rule of this register and applied in practice: a dependency change reopens its acceptance, superseded builds are marked superseded rather than deleted, and on 2026-09-10 every row was re-assessed against shipping code with stale claims corrected. Earlier candidate builds remain recorded as superseded with their failures preserved.</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-13 release notes and capability contract users see delivered limits and verified platform support"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-13</div><div><strong>Release notes and capability contract</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Users see delivered limits and verified platform support.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). The verified build record states what the build delivers, its digests, and its known limits including the eight-step assistant pause, web-only rendering and the untested two-window native case (LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md). Remaining: this is a repository record rather than release notes visible to a user inside the application.</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="z-14 full working-day acceptance named industry scenario completes create-to-handover-to-reopen with proof"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Z-14</div><div><strong>Full working-day acceptance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Named industry scenario completes create-to-handover-to-reopen with proof.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No named industry scenario has completed the create-to-handover-to-reopen working day. Handover cannot complete while external delivery is unavailable (V-05) and complete-context backup acceptance remains open (B-09). All 68 industry profiles remain not-tested.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-SO" data-category="SO"><div class="cathead"><h2>SO — Set-out and discrete optimisation</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a> · <a href="https://www.rib-software.com/en/rib-costx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RIB CostX</a> · <a href="https://www.solidworks.com/product/solidworks-design" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">SOLIDWORKS Design</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="so-01 modular division and bay set-out a run divides into bays within a maximum spacing and the remainder is resolved by a stated rule"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>SO-01</div><div><strong>Modular division and bay set-out</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: A run divides into bays within a maximum spacing and the remainder is resolved by a stated rule.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). No bay-division solver exists. The rule differs by construction system: modular systems take maximum full bays plus one cut bay at a terminal, while stick-built systems equalise all bays within maximum post centres. Blocks fencing T-1, T-3 and balustrade set-out.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="so-02 stock nesting and cut-list packing required lengths pack into orderable stock with reported offcuts and no silent rounding"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>SO-02</div><div><strong>Stock nesting and cut-list packing</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Required lengths pack into orderable stock with reported offcuts and no silent rounding.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). No 1D packing solver exists. T-11 stock lengths, packs and wastage is partial and records stock quantities, but does not pack required cuts into orderable increments. Blocks roofing T-2 and fencing material ordering.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="so-03 sheet, panel and roll layout surface elements set out for cover width, laps and staggered joints with cut waste reported"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>SO-03</div><div><strong>Sheet, panel and roll layout</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Surface elements set out for cover width, laps and staggered joints with cut waste reported.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). No 2D layout solver exists. Blocks roofing T-2 and any cladding, flooring or lining layout.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="so-04 true surface geometric development plan projections develop to true lengths and areas for a stated pitch, including unequal-pitch intersections"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>SO-04</div><div><strong>True surface geometric development</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Plan projections develop to true lengths and areas for a stated pitch, including unequal-pitch intersections.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). Plan-to-true-area development is not implemented. Unequal-pitch hip and valley true lengths are the specific case the roofing specification identified as the common error source. Blocks roofing T-1&#39;s development step.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="so-05 slope set-out and clearance solver stepping or raking is chosen against a stated threshold and resulting ground gaps are reported"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>SO-05</div><div><strong>Slope set-out and clearance solver</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Stepping or raking is chosen against a stated threshold and resulting ground gaps are reported.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). T-05 volumes, slopes and elevations is partial and treats slope as a measurement, not as a set-out input. No ground-line model, raking limit or clearance computation exists. Blocks fencing T-3.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-PH" data-category="PH"><div class="cathead"><h2>PH — Phasing, existing fabric and demolition</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.graphisoft.com/en-us/plans-and-products/archicad-collaborate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Graphisoft Archicad Collaborate</a> · <a href="https://help.autodesk.com/cloudhelp/2026/ENU/Revit-MEPEng/files/GUID-195C2C6C-5E2C-422E-A44D-FB3FDFDE276A.htm" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Revit MEP documentation</a> · <a href="https://www.procore.com/project-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Procore Project Management</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="ph-01 element lifecycle status existing, demolished, new and repaired elements stay visually and quantitatively distinct"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>PH-01</div><div><strong>Element lifecycle status</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Existing, demolished, new and repaired elements stay visually and quantitatively distinct.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). No phase, lifecycle or element-status concept exists in the model schema. Quantities cannot be split between retained and new work. Blocks residential T-1, fencing T-2 and roofing T-4.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="ph-02 demolition and strip-out scheduling removed work reports disposal, salvage and hazardous allowances separately from new work"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>PH-02</div><div><strong>Demolition and strip-out scheduling</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Removed work reports disposal, salvage and hazardous allowances separately from new work.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). No demolition scope, disposal quantity or hazardous-material allowance exists. Blocks roofing T-4 re-roof pricing, where strip and disposal are a major cost line.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="ph-03 existing interface and tie-in matching legacy profiles and tie-in points are recorded with any substitution mismatch disclosed"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>PH-03</div><div><strong>Existing interface and tie-in matching</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Legacy profiles and tie-in points are recorded with any substitution mismatch disclosed.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). No means of recording an existing product identity so a later repair can match it, and no substitution-mismatch disclosure. Blocks fencing T-2, where the existing product is frequently discontinued.</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section></div></section>
