opers, owners and project controls</option><option value="IND-60">Building certification and inspection</option><option value="IND-61">Insurance, loss assessment and forensic work</option><option value="IND-62">Education, research and training</option><option value="IND-63">Healthcare, laboratories and clean facilities</option><option value="IND-64">Data centres and critical facilities</option><option value="IND-65">Retail, hospitality and multi-site rollouts</option><option value="IND-66">Warehousing, logistics and industrial estates</option><option value="IND-67">Shipbuilding and marine fabrication</option><option value="IND-68">Recycling, waste and circular construction</option></select></label><label>Category<select id="category"><option value="">All A–Z categories</option><option value="A">A — Administration, accounts and access</option><option value="B">B — Backups, saving and project lifecycle</option><option value="C">C — CAD precision and drawing tools</option><option value="D">D — Documents, sheets and drawing registers</option><option value="E">E — Estimation, pricing and commercial work</option><option value="F">F — Field work, construction and site delivery</option><option value="G">G — Geospatial, surveying and reality capture</option><option value="H">H — HVAC, hydraulics, plumbing and fire services</option><option value="I">I — Interoperability, imports and integrations</option><option value="J">J — Jobs, programmes and commercial administration</option><option value="K">K — Knowledge, libraries and reusable standards</option><option value="L">L — Landscape, land development and public realm</option><option value="M">M — Manufacturing, mechanical design and fabrication</option><option value="N">N — Networks, electrical, controls and communications</option><option value="O">O — Operations, facilities and asset management</option><option value="P">P — Procurement, products and pricing research</option><option value="Q">Q — Quality, checking, compliance and proof</option><option value="R">R — Review, visualization and coordination</option><option value="S">S — Structural and specialist engineering</option><option value="T">T — Takeoff, measurement and quantities</option><option value="U">U — Usability, performance and everyday flexibility</option><option value="V">V — Versioning, collaboration and staff handoff</option><option value="W">W — Whole-life performance, sustainability and risk</option><option value="X">X — Extensibility, automation and AI assistance</option><option value="Y">Y — Yards, infrastructure, industrial and specialist assets</option><option value="Z">Z — Zero-loss delivery, release and business continuity</option><option value="SO">SO — Set-out and discrete optimisation</option><option value="PH">PH — Phasing, existing fabric and demolition</option></select></label><button id="reset" type="button">Reset</button></div><p id="results" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><nav aria-label="A to Z category index"><a href="#category-A">A</a><a href="#category-B">B</a><a href="#category-C">C</a><a href="#category-D">D</a><a href="#category-E">E</a><a href="#category-F">F</a><a href="#category-G">G</a><a href="#category-H">H</a><a href="#category-I">I</a><a href="#category-J">J</a><a href="#category-K">K</a><a href="#category-L">L</a><a href="#category-M">M</a><a href="#category-N">N</a><a href="#category-O">O</a><a href="#category-P">P</a><a href="#category-Q">Q</a><a href="#category-R">R</a><a href="#category-S">S</a><a href="#category-T">T</a><a href="#category-U">U</a><a href="#category-V">V</a><a href="#category-W">W</a><a href="#category-X">X</a><a href="#category-Y">Y</a><a href="#category-Z">Z</a><a href="#category-SO">SO</a><a href="#category-PH">PH</a></nav><div id="requirements"><section class="category" id="category-A" data-category="A"><div class="cathead"><h2>A — Administration, accounts and access</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://helpcenter.graphisoft.com/user-guide/134439/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Graphisoft BIMcloud teams</a> · <a href="https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Forma construction document management</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="a-01 organization workspaces two companies cannot read each other&#39;s project records"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-01</div><div><strong>Organization workspaces</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Two companies cannot read each other&#39;s project records.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no organisation or tenant model; project records are local to one profile. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-02 individual sign-in and sign-out sign-out removes access and cached private views"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-02</div><div><strong>Individual sign-in and sign-out</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Sign-out removes access and cached private views.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). A Better Auth server with federated providers exists but ships disabled, email and password sign-in is switched off in code and no sign-in or sign-out forms are built (`src/lib/auth/`). With authentication off the app resolves a development identity, so sign-out behaviour cannot be assessed. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-03 staff invitations an accepted invitation grants only the invited role"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-03</div><div><strong>Staff invitations</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: An accepted invitation grants only the invited role.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no invitation model. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-04 project roles viewer cannot edit; estimator cannot approve engineering"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-04</div><div><strong>Project roles</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Viewer cannot edit; estimator cannot approve engineering.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no project role model. The assistant permission mode governs tool execution, not user roles, and must not be read as satisfying this row. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-05 document and field permissions restricted rates remain hidden in screens and exports"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-05</div><div><strong>Document and field permissions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Restricted rates remain hidden in screens and exports.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no field-level permission, so restricted rates cannot be hidden in screens or exports. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-06 external guest access guest sees only explicitly shared packages"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-06</div><div><strong>External guest access</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Guest sees only explicitly shared packages.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no guest access or shared package. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-07 access revocation previously valid links and sessions lose access when revoked"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-07</div><div><strong>Access revocation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Previously valid links and sessions lose access when revoked.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no session or link revocation. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-08 multi-factor and enterprise identity enforced identity policy survives account recovery"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-08</div><div><strong>Multi-factor and enterprise identity</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Enforced identity policy survives account recovery.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Federated sign-in through a broker is scaffolded for two providers, but multi-factor policy and account recovery are not implemented and authentication is disabled by default (`src/lib/auth/providers.ts`). — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-09 staff directory and teams reassignment preserves historical authorship"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-09</div><div><strong>Staff directory and teams</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reassignment preserves historical authorship.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no staff directory, so authorship cannot survive reassignment. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-10 audit trail actor, time, action and affected revision are recorded"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-10</div><div><strong>Audit trail</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Actor, time, action and affected revision are recorded.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Assistant actions are journalled with work packets and raw task events, and takeoff evidence approval records a named reviewer with a timestamp (`src/studio/assistant/workPacketStore.ts`; SC-12 journey approved evidence for a named person). Remaining: there is no application-wide audit trail of actor, time, action and affected revision, and with no accounts the actor is not an authenticated identity. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-11 account recovery and offboarding removed staff cannot retain active organization access"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-11</div><div><strong>Account recovery and offboarding</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Removed staff cannot retain active organization access.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). No account service is selected and authentication ships disabled by default, so this row cannot be assessed. There is no offboarding path. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-12 regional settings units, currency, date and timezone are explicit per project"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-12</div><div><strong>Regional settings</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Units, currency, date and timezone are explicit per project.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Units are fixed to millimetres by schema and currency is ISO-4217 validated per price book with an effective date and tax basis (`src/studio/architect/model.ts`, `priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: regional settings are not explicit or editable per project, and date and timezone handling is not declared. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-13 custom fields and classifications required fields validate and survive export/import"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-13</div><div><strong>Custom fields and classifications</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Required fields validate and survive export/import.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no user-defined custom fields or classifications, so validation and survival through export and import cannot be assessed. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="a-14 organization templates template revisions do not silently alter existing projects"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>A-14</div><div><strong>Organization templates</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Template revisions do not silently alter existing projects.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no organisation templates, so no template revision can alter an existing project. This is blocked behind the same missing account and organisation model as the rest of category A. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-B" data-category="B"><div class="cathead"><h2>B — Backups, saving and project lifecycle</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://construction.autodesk.com/workflows/construction-document-management/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Forma construction document management</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="b-01 create and name projects unique ids survive duplicate display names"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Checked">✓</span>B-01</div><div><strong>Create and name projects</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Unique IDs survive duplicate display names.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (reviewed by Codex 2026-09-11, built browser on DANS1). The Project library creates and reopens two identically named projects with distinct IDs. Code: src/studio/ProjectLibrary.tsx, src/studio/projectRegistry.ts. Exact patch, 34 tests, dev/production journeys, fixture/build hashes and inspected desktop/tablet screenshots: proof/growth/2026-09-11-project-library/README.md. No installed/native platform claim.</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-02 automatic save feedback saved appears only after durable storage succeeds"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-02</div><div><strong>Automatic save feedback</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Saved appears only after durable storage succeeds.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Re-verified in development 2026-09-08 for the main project record: &quot;saved · revision N&quot; appears only after a readback-verified write; an injected quota failure shows &quot;not confirmed saved&quot; with a retry that succeeds once storage recovers. Code/proof: [SC-02 protected saves](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-protected-saves/README.md), [walkthrough](walkthrough.md). Remaining: per-module records, production/native build. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-03 save as and duplicate copy gets new identity without sharing mutable records"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-03</div><div><strong>Save As and duplicate</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Copy gets new identity without sharing mutable records.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no Save As or duplicate action. The registry can shelve and switch projects but does not fork one into a new identity with independent mutable records. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-04 reopen recent projects latest saved revision and source sheets return after restart"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-04</div><div><strong>Reopen recent projects</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Latest saved revision and source sheets return after restart.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (updated 2026-09-11). Project library lists saved projects and reopens the exact project ID, revision 2 and original drawing after page reload, archive and restore. Code: src/studio/ProjectLibrary.tsx. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-project-library/README.md. Remaining: full browser-process/installed-app restart with the same source fixture; a page reload is not that test. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-05 offline local storage airplane-mode restart restores drawings and attached originals"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-05</div><div><strong>Offline local storage</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Airplane-mode restart restores drawings and attached originals.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Storage is local first: drawings, price books and attached originals persist in browser storage and IndexedDB with no network dependency, and a 9.3 MB backup was captured and read back in a live journey (SC-10). Remaining: an airplane-mode restart has not been executed as a declared scenario. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-06 cross-device project storage authorized second device opens the same confirmed revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-06</div><div><strong>Cross-device project storage</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Authorized second device opens the same confirmed revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no cross-device storage. Persistence is local to one browser profile or one desktop install, and no account service is selected. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-07 archive and restore projects archived jobs leave the active list and restore intact"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Checked">✓</span>B-07</div><div><strong>Archive and restore projects</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Archived jobs leave the active list and restore intact.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (reviewed by Codex 2026-09-11, built browser on DANS1). Archive hides inactive projects and assistant tabs; restore retains the original project ID, revision, source records and SHA-256-verified drawing bytes. Only the registry marker changes; stored project data is preserved. Current, unreadable and stale targets are refused. Code: src/studio/projectArchive.ts, src/studio/ProjectLibrary.tsx, src/studio/assistant/projectSwitch.ts. Exact diff, executed failure-path tests and inspected desktop/tablet proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-project-library/README.md. Portable backup restoration remains B-09; installed/native acceptance is separate.</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-08 recycle bin accidental removal is recoverable with links and history intact"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-08</div><div><strong>Recycle bin</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Accidental removal is recoverable with links and history intact.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no recycle bin. Source-page archive and recover is the nearest behaviour and is assessed under D-04 and D-05. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-09 portable complete backup restore on a clean profile includes sources, models, rates and evidence"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-09</div><div><strong>Portable complete backup</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Restore on a clean profile includes sources, models, rates and evidence.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (reviewed 2026-09-11). V2 restoration now runs before editor hydration under an exclusive workspace lease, with an immutable incoming package, recovery copy, validated before/after journal, non-overwriting originals and active job switched last. A transferred package restores an exact project revision and original SVG SHA-256 in a fresh browser context. Code: src/studio/workspaceRestoreStorage.ts, src/studio/workspaceRestorePlan.ts, src/studio/WorkspaceStartup.tsx. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-restore/README.md. Remaining: complete sources/models/rates/evidence fixture coverage, excluded assistant/runtime/model-preference context, installed/native and clean-machine acceptance. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-10 backup integrity preview corrupt or missing assets block replacement before any write"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Checked">✓</span>B-10</div><div><strong>Backup integrity preview</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Corrupt or missing assets block replacement before any write.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (reviewed by Codex 2026-09-11, built browser on DANS1). Packages, original identities and destination fingerprints are revalidated before staging and again before protected application. Corrupt originals introduced after review refuse the real restore action, preserve the active record and retain conflicting source bytes. Missing/corrupt package assets and source collisions are also covered by executed tests. Code: src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts, src/studio/workspaceRestoreStorage.ts, src/studio/BackupRestoreReview.tsx. Exact patch, 45 tests, production browser receipts and inspected screenshots: proof/growth/2026-09-11-restore/README.md. Native acceptance and full-project coverage remain separate.</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-11 crash and interrupted-write recovery last confirmed snapshot survives forced termination"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-11</div><div><strong>Crash and interrupted-write recovery</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Last confirmed snapshot survives forced termination.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (reviewed 2026-09-11). Backup restore now journals before-images and recovers prepared/writing phases before editor hydration; ambiguous save acknowledgements stop writes and replay the durable phase on reload. Injected module failures and simulated persisted interruption pass, including browser rollback and damaged-journal refusal. Code: src/studio/workspaceRestore.ts, src/studio/WorkspaceStartup.tsx. Proof: proof/growth/2026-09-11-restore/README.md. Remaining: actual forced process termination mid-write, mixed-version windows and native recovery drills are not proved. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-12 concurrent edit protection stale writer cannot silently overwrite a newer revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-12</div><div><strong>Concurrent edit protection</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Stale writer cannot silently overwrite a newer revision.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Main project record protected in development 2026-09-08: compare-and-swap against the last loaded/written bytes refuses a stale write and leaves the newer stored revision byte-identical; a cross-window storage event pauses saving with a &quot;newer revision exists&quot; notice offering reload and a download of the unsaved revision; reload adopts the newer revision. 49 focused tests, same-window, two-tab and reload-failure Fast CDP proof, three independent verifiers not refuted. Code/proof: [SC-02 protected saves](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-protected-saves/README.md). Remaining: per-module records (BOM, inventory, architecture, price books, sheet metadata), Web Lock lease, production/native build. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-13 storage failure recovery full disk/quota error preserves previous data and supports retry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-13</div><div><strong>Storage failure recovery</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Full disk/quota error preserves previous data and supports retry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Main project record verified in development 2026-09-08: quota throw and silent-write failures keep the previously stored bytes byte-identical and the in-memory edit; an explicit retry persists it (store test plus tablet 1024x768 Fast CDP proof). Code/proof: [SC-02 protected saves](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-protected-saves/README.md). Remaining: IndexedDB originals/materials and per-module records, production/native build. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="b-14 migration and retention older supported backups upgrade with a reversible audit record"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>B-14</div><div><strong>Migration and retention</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Older supported backups upgrade with a reversible audit record.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A supported legacy schema migrates forward and an unsupported one fails closed with the original bytes preserved, asserted by test (`src/studio/persistence.ts`). Remaining: migration is not reversible and produces no audit record, which is the substance of this row. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-C" data-category="C"><div class="cathead"><h2>C — CAD precision and drawing tools</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="c-01 lines, polylines, arcs and circles exact coordinates survive save and cad exchange"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-01</div><div><strong>Lines, polylines, arcs and circles</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Exact coordinates survive save and CAD exchange.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Lines, arcs and circles are authored entities and survive a hash-bound DXF round trip that restores stable IDs exactly (`src/studio/architect/model.ts`, `exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts` &quot;DXF parametric round trip preserves stable IDs&quot;). A general open polyline entity does not exist: an imported LWPOLYLINE is exploded into separate lines. Remaining: a polyline entity, and coordinate survival through DWG and IFC rather than DXF alone. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-02 splines and curves control points and curve tolerance survive supported exchanges"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-02</div><div><strong>Splines and curves</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Control points and curve tolerance survive supported exchanges.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No spline or NURBS entity exists in the model schema. Curved geometry is limited to circles and arcs. There is nothing to assess until a curve type is authored. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-03 object snaps and tracking endpoint, midpoint, perpendicular and intersection picks are correct"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-03</div><div><strong>Object snaps and tracking</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Endpoint, midpoint, perpendicular and intersection picks are correct.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Seven snap kinds are computed geometrically and each is asserted independently, including line-circle and circle-circle intersections and a tangent at an irrational point (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts` snapPoint; `architect.test.ts` &quot;snap candidates resolve endpoint, midpoint, intersection, perpendicular, extension, centre and tangent&quot;; 72 tests logged 2026-09-10). Remaining: no inspected screenshot of live cursor snapping at the declared viewports, so the row stays partial under the tick rule. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-04 numeric and relative entry typed distance/angle yields the expected measured geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-04</div><div><strong>Numeric and relative entry</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Typed distance/angle yields the expected measured geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Typed length with ortho and polar angle stepping resolves to the exact constrained distance (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts` constrainPoint, asserted at 4500 mm on a 30 degree polar step). Remaining: typed angle and absolute or relative coordinate entry are not implemented, and there is no visual proof. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-05 coordinate systems and origins local and project origins transform without drift"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-05</div><div><strong>Coordinate systems and origins</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Local and project origins transform without drift.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). A single global millimetre space with level elevations is implemented. There is no user coordinate system, origin relocation or rotated working plane, so the row cannot be assessed. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-06 layers and visibility hidden, locked and isolated layers retain correct entity membership"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-06</div><div><strong>Layers and visibility</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Hidden, locked and isolated layers retain correct entity membership.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No CAD drafting layer exists. The model field named layers is a wall assembly material layer, not a visibility or lock container, and DXF export synthesises layer names from levels. Recorded explicitly because the field name invites a false positive. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-07 selection and properties window/crossing selection and batch edits affect intended objects only"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-07</div><div><strong>Selection and properties</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Window/crossing selection and batch edits affect intended objects only.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Selection is a single entity id. Window and crossing selection, multi-select and batch property edits are not implemented. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-08 move, rotate, scale and copy transform and undo preserve dimensions and ids"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-08</div><div><strong>Move, rotate, scale and copy</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Transform and undo preserve dimensions and IDs.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Move, rotate, scale, copy and array are not implemented as transforms. Offset and mirror each derive one copy, which does not satisfy this row. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-09 offset, trim, extend and fillet edge cases retain valid connected geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-09</div><div><strong>Offset, trim, extend and fillet</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Edge cases retain valid connected geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Offset, mirror, trim, extend and a tangential fillet are real solvers with asserted results and explicit edge-case refusals: a radius too large for its segments, parallel segments that cannot meet, and an intersection already inside the segment are each rejected with a stated reason (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts`; `architect.test.ts` &quot;precision exact length, mirror, offset, trim, extend and tangential fillet&quot;). Remaining: no inspected screenshot, and connected-geometry survival is proven per operation rather than across a drawing session. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-10 blocks and reusable symbols definition update changes intended instances without broken attributes"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-10</div><div><strong>Blocks and reusable symbols</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Definition update changes intended instances without broken attributes.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No block, symbol or instance definition exists. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-11 constraints and parameters driving dimension regenerates dependent geometry consistently"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-11</div><div><strong>Constraints and parameters</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Driving dimension regenerates dependent geometry consistently.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No geometric or dimensional constraint solver exists. Wall-hosted dimensions report geometry; they do not drive it. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-12 dimensions, leaders and text annotation values update and plot legibly at scale"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-12</div><div><strong>Dimensions, leaders and text</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Annotation values update and plot legibly at scale.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Wall-hosted dimensions are associative: moving a wall end from 4000 to 5000 mm regenerates the annotation text, and plan, elevation and section views regenerate with it (`src/studio/architect/drawing.ts`; `architect.test.ts` &quot;plan, elevations, sections and associative dimensions regenerate after editing&quot;). Remaining: free-standing linear, aligned, angular and radial dimensions, leaders and user-placed text do not exist, and plotted legibility at scale is unproven. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-13 hatches, lineweights and plot styles screen and exported output agree on declared styles"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-13</div><div><strong>Hatches, lineweights and plot styles</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Screen and exported output agree on declared styles.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Hatching is genuine scanline geometry with ring containment and hole exclusion across five patterns, and per-primitive widths are emitted for plan, elevation and section output (`src/studio/architect/drawing.ts` hatchLines). Remaining: no user control of lineweight, colour or plot style, and no proof that screen and exported PDF agree on declared styles. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="c-14 undo, redo and transaction history one user operation undoes atomically without losing active context"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>C-14</div><div><strong>Undo, redo and transaction history</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: One user operation undoes atomically without losing active context.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Undo and redo form a two-stack history capped at 60 steps with redo invalidated on a new edit, bound to Ctrl+Z and Ctrl+Y, and one architect operation is one transaction (`src/studio/architect/ArchitectWorkspace.tsx`). The assistant undo path is separately proven in the SC-08 journeys. Remaining: history is cleared on project load, so undo does not survive a reopen, and no inspected screenshot covers the keyboard path. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-D" data-category="D"><div class="cathead"><h2>D — Documents, sheets and drawing registers</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a> · <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="d-01 multi-file and multi-page import pdfs with different page sizes preserve every original page"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-01</div><div><strong>Multi-file and multi-page import</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: PDFs with different page sizes preserve every original page.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Multi-page PDF import stores each page with its own identity and dimensions, and a 13-page Redburn set was imported and retained through native runs (SC-10, SC-13). Remaining: a fixture with deliberately mixed page sizes has not been asserted page by page. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-02 sheet names and numbers rename changes labels without breaking evidence references"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-02</div><div><strong>Sheet names and numbers</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Rename changes labels without breaking evidence references.</p><small class="muted">State: partial — verified in development 2026-09-08 for source sheets: rename changes only the page label/discipline; calibrations, traces, items, annotations and saved views stay keyed by original page index and byte-identical; the new name shows in the register, heading and navigation after reload. Fixture Redburn BR250157 (SHA-256 b57956f76b5dc893ac2b28a021f3f92e345807e326d6b1f8313e373f9145ad38, 13 pages); 37 focused tests; three verifiers not refuted. Code/proof: [SC-03 sheets](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-sheets/README.md). Remaining: authored architectural sheets, production/native build. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-03 add and duplicate drawing sheets new sheet receives an independent identity and layout"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-03</div><div><strong>Add and duplicate drawing sheets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: New sheet receives an independent identity and layout.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Authored sheets can be added, duplicated, renamed, reordered, archived and recovered, each with an independent identity and layout, and duplication does not share viewport records (`src/studio/architect/authoredSheetSet.ts`, tests pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: no inspected screenshot of the authored sheet lifecycle at the declared viewports. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-04 remove with impact preview review lists dependent takeoffs, links and viewports before removal"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-04</div><div><strong>Remove with impact preview</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Review lists dependent takeoffs, links and viewports before removal.</p><small class="muted">State: partial — verified in development 2026-09-08 for source-page archive (the product&#39;s removal): the review lists calibrations, measured traces, located items, annotations, linked photos and, newly, saved views for that page, and storage stays unchanged until confirmation. Code/proof: [SC-03 sheets](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-sheets/README.md). Remaining: whole-source removal, SHA-bound construction takeoff registers (not page-scoped, so not counted), production/native build. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-05 restore removed sheets restored sheet recovers annotations, scale and original ordering"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-05</div><div><strong>Restore removed sheets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Restored sheet recovers annotations, scale and original ordering.</p><small class="muted">State: partial — verified in development 2026-09-08 as archive → recover: the page returns to its original managed slot with identical metadata, its locked scale and a real sketch annotation byte-identical after recover and reload (unit test with job evidence after archive and recover; browser assertions on 13 calibrations and the annotation at every step). Code/proof: [SC-03 sheets](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-sheets/README.md). Remaining: authored sheets, production/native build. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-06 reorder and group sheets discipline groups and order persist after restart and export"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-06</div><div><strong>Reorder and group sheets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Discipline groups and order persist after restart and export.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for source-sheet discipline groups, persistent managed order and an actual ordered-register download, retaining every original page identity through reload in browser and Windows-native runs. Remaining: the export is a JSON register, and authored multi-sheet publishing and reordering the source PDF itself are outside that acceptance. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-07 title blocks and templates project metadata updates linked fields without clipping"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-07</div><div><strong>Title blocks and templates</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Project metadata updates linked fields without clipping.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (re-assessed 2026-09-11). Corrected from gap: the 2026-09-10 assessment stated that project metadata cannot update linked fields, and that is wrong. A title block is drawn on every authored sheet and its fields are already linked to project metadata: project name, address, sheet number, design revision, paper size, model revision, a rotating north arrow driven by the sheet&#39;s northAngle, and a scale bar computed from the sheet scale (`src/studio/architect/ArchitectSheets.tsx`, the title strip below the frame; `authoredSheetSet.ts` holds number and northAngle per sheet; 21/21 architect tests pass 2026-09-11). Remaining, and the reason this is not verified: the block is hardcoded at fixed coordinates with no template concept, so its content and layout cannot be chosen, no firm or client title block can be substituted, and there is the fit is now proven at the maximum stored lengths (name 200, address 500) both on screen and in the exported PDF. The exported drawing is fitted with the embedded font&#39;s own metrics: at the schema maximum a 500 character address is drawn as 213 characters with a truncation marker on A3 and in full on A1, read back from the PDF content stream rather than asserted (proof/growth/2026-09-11-d13-export/README.md, pdf-text-verification.log; 51/51 tests). Remaining: no template system, so the block&#39;s content and layout cannot be chosen and no firm or client title block can be substituted; and no inspected screenshot of the PDF itself, because Chrome&#39;s PDF plugin does not expose its render surface to CDP here. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-08 viewports and per-view scale independent scales measure correctly in exported pdf"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-08</div><div><strong>Viewports and per-view scale</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Independent scales measure correctly in exported PDF.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A sheet carries up to twelve viewports with independent view, level, scale and position, and resizing the paper refits frames without altering viewport scales (`src/studio/architect/authoredSheetSet.ts`). Export is real vector PDF (`sheets.ts`). Remaining: measuring an exported PDF at each declared viewport scale has not been executed. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-09 drawing revisions and supersession old revision remains retrievable and visibly superseded"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-09</div><div><strong>Drawing revisions and supersession</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Old revision remains retrievable and visibly superseded.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-12). Implemented: issue sets record immutable historical issue records and frozen sheet layouts with deterministic SHA-256 layout hashing and design revision tracking (`src/studio/architect/issueHistory.ts`, `model.ts`, `ArchitectSheets.tsx`). When a new revision is issued (e.g. Rev B), prior current issues automatically transition to `superseded` status with timestamps and pointers to the successor revision (`supersededByRevision: &quot;B&quot;`). The Drawing sheets tab displays an expandable &quot;Drawing revisions &amp; history&quot; control with `CURRENT` and `SUPERSEDED` status badges and an issue register table. Clicking &quot;Inspect layout&quot; on an older revision retrieves the frozen layout onto the canvas stage, with a prominent `.arch-superseded-banner` alert and a diagonal semi-transparent red `SUPERSEDED` SVG watermark across the paper drawing, while locking viewport and sheet editing controls. Proven by 8 unit tests covering issue recording, stale-review refusal, supersession transitions, retrievability of modified/deleted sheets, and chronological lineage (92/92 architect tests passing, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0), plus an inspected Fast CDP browser scenario (`proof/growth/2026-09-12-d09-revisions/README.md`, `fast-cdp-execution.log`, 3 screenshots at 1680×1050). Remaining, and why this is not verified: development browser only, with no production minification build, no installed desktop package run, and no tablet capture; revision lineage is single-sequence rather than multi-party branching; and historical issues are persisted in client project state / LocalStorage rather than a central cloud-synced revision vault. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-10 revision overlay and slip-sheeting added/deleted geometry is inspectable with alignment controls"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-10</div><div><strong>Revision overlay and slip-sheeting</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Added/deleted geometry is inspectable with alignment controls.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision overlay or slip-sheeting, so added and deleted geometry cannot be inspected between issues. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-11 ocr and sheet indexing suggested names are reviewable and uncertainty is visible"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-11</div><div><strong>OCR and sheet indexing</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Suggested names are reviewable and uncertainty is visible.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no OCR or automatic sheet indexing, and therefore no suggested names or visible uncertainty. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-12 cross-sheet references and hyperlinks detail callout opens the intended sheet revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-12</div><div><strong>Cross-sheet references and hyperlinks</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Detail callout opens the intended sheet revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Cross-sheet references and detail callouts are not implemented. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-13 batch printing and issue sets selected sheets export in reviewed order with an issue register"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-13</div><div><strong>Batch printing and issue sets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Selected sheets export in reviewed order with an issue register.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-12). Implemented: selected sheets are issued as one PDF whose first page is a drawing issue register listing every sheet in printed order with its number, size, scale and viewport count, plus the issue purpose, design revision, model revision and timestamp. Order follows the design&#39;s managed sheet order rather than click order, so the issued set matches the register the user reads on screen. An issue is reviewed before export and the review is refused if the design changed after it, in the UI and again inside the export function so a programmatic caller cannot bypass it. Each sheet renders through the existing single-sheet path and the pages are merged, so an issued drawing is the drawing the user saw, and mixed A1/A3 paper sizes survive (`src/studio/architect/issueSet.ts`, `sheets.ts` exportIssueSetPdf, `ArchitectSheets.tsx`). Proven by reading a committed 5-page issue back from its own bytes and by an inspected desktop browser journey covering selection, review and the stale-review refusal; 73/73 tests, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0 (proof/growth/2026-09-12-d13-issue-set/README.md). Remaining, and why this is not verified: development-server browser only, with no built-browser or installed-app run and no tablet capture; the browser proof does not exercise the file download itself; and no issue history is stored, so the project holds no record of what was issued when, which D-09 supersession would need. Single-sheet PDF export remains assessed under D-08. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-14 bookmarks and saved views personal navigation restores the correct page and viewport"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-14</div><div><strong>Bookmarks and saved views</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Personal navigation restores the correct page and viewport.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for local original-page, zoom and source-relative-centre bookmarks, with pan, zoom, page switching, viewport restoration, resize, reload, removal and failed-write preservation passing, and a tablet sub-check at both declared orientations. Remaining: saved views are local project metadata, with no account synchronisation or sharing. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="d-15 visual and vector revision delta two issued revisions report added, removed and changed geometry with a quantity variance table"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>D-15</div><div><strong>Visual and vector revision delta</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Two issued revisions report added, removed and changed geometry with a quantity variance table.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-12). Implemented: pure revision delta comparison engine (`src/studio/architect/revisionDelta.ts`) and project geometry snapshot capture on drawing issue (`src/studio/architect/issueHistory.ts`, `model.ts`). When an issue set is exported, a frozen geometry snapshot of project levels, walls, hosted openings, slabs, roofs, and annotations is saved alongside the sheet layouts. In the Drawing sheets tab (`src/studio/architect/ArchitectSheets.tsx`), an interactive &quot;Compare revisions (Revision Delta)&quot; panel enables instant comparison between any two issued revisions (e.g. Rev A vs Rev B) or between an issue and live WIP design. Reports: (1) high-level KPI cards for sheet modifications, geometry changes, net area variance, and material cost delta; (2) color-coded delta cards for added, removed, and modified sheets (detecting size, scale, and layout hash differences); (3) vector geometry element delta cards tracking modified wall lengths/alignments/layers, hosted door/window parameters (sill, hinge, swing, dimensions), slabs, and roofs; and (4) an interactive Quantity Variance Schedule with trade/material breakdowns, unit of measurement, baseline vs target quantities, delta (Δ) with color-coded badges, and percentage change. Proven by 7 unit tests (99/99 architect tests passing, `tsc --noEmit` exit 0) and an inspected Fast CDP browser scenario (`proof/growth/2026-09-12-d15-delta/README.md`, `fast-cdp-execution.log`, 3 screenshots at 1680×1050). Remaining, and why this is not verified: development browser only, with no production minification build, no installed desktop package run, and no tablet capture; geometry delta uses element ID and parameter diffing rather than raster pixel-diff shaders or 3D mesh boolean intersection; and historical issues and snapshots are persisted in client project state / LocalStorage rather than a central cloud-synced revision vault. Review corrections 2026-09-12: legacy geometry now fails closed, missed element/layout changes are detected, and slab/roof detail cards are complete. Machine tests pass; full interaction proof remains pending. Prior annotation-comparison and legacy-fallback claims are superseded by proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md. Review corrections 2026-09-12: legacy geometry now fails closed, missed element/layout changes are detected, and slab/roof detail cards are complete. Machine tests pass; full interaction proof remains pending. Prior annotation-comparison and legacy-fallback claims are superseded by proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-E" data-category="E"><div class="cathead"><h2>E — Estimation, pricing and commercial work</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.rib-software.com/en/rib-costx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RIB CostX</a> · <a href="https://oneclicklca.com/en-gb/software/design-construction/life-cycle-costing" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">One Click LCA life-cycle costing</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="e-01 pricing workbook import xlsx/csv sheets preview without executing spreadsheet formulas"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-01</div><div><strong>Pricing workbook import</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: XLSX/CSV sheets preview without executing spreadsheet formulas.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for bounded XLSX and CSV preview with no spreadsheet formula execution: a mapped formula is refused despite a cached value, malformed input is preserved, and reload passes in the declared browser and Windows scenarios (`src/studio/priceWorkbook.ts`). Remaining: a 2 MiB source and 20 MiB expanded archive limit, no XLS, XLSM or encrypted files, and the rates used were QA fixtures rather than supplier quotations. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-02 column and worksheet mapping sku, description, unit and rate map with row-level errors"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-02</div><div><strong>Column and worksheet mapping</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: SKU, description, unit and rate map with row-level errors.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Verified in the 2026-09-07 acceptance addendum in this file for worksheet and heading selection and SKU, description, unit and rate mapping with row and cell errors, where explicit review precedes saving and the source hash, selected worksheet and physical rows survive reload (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: no inferred currency or unit conversion, and the original workbook bytes are not embedded in backups. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-03 named price books and revisions supplier revisions coexist and old estimates remain reproducible"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-03</div><div><strong>Named price books and revisions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Supplier revisions coexist and old estimates remain reproducible.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Price books are append-only and revisioned so supplier revisions coexist and an earlier revision remains readable, with archive supported and a live CSV import creating a named book at library revision 1 (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`; SC-12 journey). Remaining: reproducing an old estimate against its original revision has not been executed. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-04 currency, tax and effective dates mixed currencies never total without a reviewed conversion"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-04</div><div><strong>Currency, tax and effective dates</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Mixed currencies never total without a reviewed conversion.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Currency is ISO-4217 validated and totals are grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places and summed in integer minor units, so mixed currencies never silently total, and an effective date and tax basis are carried per book (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: there is no reviewed conversion path, so mixed currencies are separated rather than converted. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-05 unit and pack normalization each/metre/square-metre/pack conversion shows its dimensional basis"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-05</div><div><strong>Unit and pack normalization</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Each/metre/square-metre/pack conversion shows its dimensional basis.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Unit is free text carried through from the source workbook. There is no unit or pack normalisation and no dimensional basis display, so the row cannot be assessed. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-06 apply and remove a price book impact preview preserves manual overrides and supports undo"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-06</div><div><strong>Apply and remove a price book</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Impact preview preserves manual overrides and supports undo.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). A price book cannot be applied to measured quantities or removed from them. Worksheet lines can be priced individually, and the quantity bridge returns an explicit unavailable status (`src/studio/crmBridge.ts`). [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-07 supplier quote comparison equal specifications compare landed cost and exclusions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-07</div><div><strong>Supplier quote comparison</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Equal specifications compare landed cost and exclusions.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Supplier quote comparison with landed cost and exclusions is not implemented. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-08 material, labour and plant build-ups assembly rate reconciles to separately editable components"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-08</div><div><strong>Material, labour and plant build-ups</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Assembly rate reconciles to separately editable components.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-19; SC-10 proof updated 2026-09-20). QS contractor revisions independently pin material and labour supplier revisions/lines, or record explicit labour exclusion; waste, markup and tax remain separate. Domain tests and the DANS1 measured-run UI reconcile AUD55 material +10 labour +13 markup +7.80 GST =85.80 for the controlled 5m base row. [Original partial evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-19-sc10-qs-rate-delta/AZ-PARTIAL-ASSESSMENT.md); [current exact-decimal workflow, tests, screenshots and diff](proof/growth/2026-09-20-sc10-use-measured/steps/SC10-USE-MEASURED-01.md), 297/297 development-browser PASS. Remaining: plant and broader assemblies, production-built/native qualification. Catalogue state remains partial; no row tick or count promotion. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-09 waste, yield and productivity assumptions remain separate from measured net quantities"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-09</div><div><strong>Waste, yield and productivity</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Assumptions remain separate from measured net quantities.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Waste is a declared percentage held separately from net measured geometry, so an order quantity never overwrites the measured demand (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`). Remaining: yield and productivity assumptions do not exist. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-10 discount, margin and contingency formula order is explicit and totals independently reconcile"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-10</div><div><strong>Discount, margin and contingency</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Formula order is explicit and totals independently reconcile.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Discount, margin and contingency are not implemented, so there is no formula order to make explicit. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-11 tender alternates and scenarios base and options compare without altering the accepted baseline"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-11</div><div><strong>Tender alternates and scenarios</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Base and options compare without altering the accepted baseline.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-19; SC-10 proof updated 2026-09-20). Proposed option AUD68.64 remains outside the AUD85.80 base/accepted total; explicitly accepting it raises the accepted total to154.44 while base stays85.80. [Original partial evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-19-sc10-qs-rate-delta/AZ-PARTIAL-ASSESSMENT.md). The [current 297/297 development-browser campaign](proof/growth/2026-09-20-sc10-use-measured/steps/SC10-USE-MEASURED-01.md) now proves four frozen revisions, changed exact geometry/rates, new/removed/modified rows, tablet and normal reload; earlier snapshot bytes stay preserved. Remaining: production-built/native acceptance. Catalogue state remains partial; no row tick or count promotion. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-12 escalation and exchange rates source and effective date bind each applied factor"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-12</div><div><strong>Escalation and exchange rates</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Source and effective date bind each applied factor.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Escalation and exchange-rate factors are not implemented. An effective date is recorded per price book but binds no applied factor. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-13 quote approval and issue issued estimate freezes rates, quantities, exclusions and revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-13</div><div><strong>Quote approval and issue</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Issued estimate freezes rates, quantities, exclusions and revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no quote approval or issue, so nothing freezes rates, quantities and exclusions. Takeoff evidence approval for a named reviewer is a separate behaviour assessed under Q-10 and V rows. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-14 cost-to-complete and variations approved changes reconcile original budget to current forecast"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-14</div><div><strong>Cost-to-complete and variations</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Approved changes reconcile original budget to current forecast.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Cost-to-complete and variation reconciliation are not implemented. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="e-15 preliminaries and site allowances time-related and site-wide costs are built up separately from measured rates and carry into the estimate without double counting"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>E-15</div><div><strong>Preliminaries and site allowances</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Time-related and site-wide costs are built up separately from measured rates and carry into the estimate without double counting.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). Added to the register on 2026-09-11 from the quantity surveying specification, which found no row for preliminaries anywhere in category E. Site establishment, scaffolding, craneage, supervision and waste are a standard separately-built estimate component; E-08 build-ups is itself a gap. Source: planning/PROPOSED-REGISTER-EXPANSIONS.md. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-F" data-category="F"><div class="cathead"><h2>F — Field work, construction and site delivery</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.procore.com/project-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Procore Project Management</a> · <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="f-01 offline field packages required drawings and checklists open without connectivity"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>F-01</div><div><strong>Offline field packages</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Required drawings and checklists open without connectivity.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no offline field package. The application itself is local-first, which is assessed under B-05, but no drawings-and-checklists package is produced for site use. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="f-02 rfis question links to exact drawing revision and tracks response/closure"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>F-02</div><div><strong>RFIs</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Question links to exact drawing revision and tracks response/closure.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no request-for-information record linked to a drawing revision. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="f-03 submittals and shop drawing review review route, due date and resubmission history persist"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>F-03</d