s="requirement" data-search="h-12 plantroom access and coordination maintenance clearances are checked against actual geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>H-12</div><div><strong>Plantroom access and coordination</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Maintenance clearances are checked against actual geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No mechanical, hydraulic, plumbing or fire-services engine exists. Duct, pipe and service words appear only as trade labels on takeoff categories and construction stages, never as sized or solved systems. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="h-13 risers, schematics and schedules changes propagate consistently between representations"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>H-13</div><div><strong>Risers, schematics and schedules</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Changes propagate consistently between representations.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No mechanical, hydraulic, plumbing or fire-services engine exists. Duct, pipe and service words appear only as trade labels on takeoff categories and construction stages, never as sized or solved systems. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="h-14 commissioning and balancing records as-tested performance links to installed equipment revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>H-14</div><div><strong>Commissioning and balancing records</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: As-tested performance links to installed equipment revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No mechanical, hydraulic, plumbing or fire-services engine exists. Duct, pipe and service words appear only as trade labels on takeoff categories and construction stages, never as sized or solved systems. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-I" data-category="I"><div class="cathead"><h2>I — Interoperability, imports and integrations</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a> · <a href="https://github.com/DomCR/ACadSharp" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ACadSharp</a> · <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/bim-collaboration-format/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART BCF</a> · <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/information-delivery-specification-ids/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART IDS</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="i-01 dxf import/export independent reader verifies supported geometry, layers and units"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-01</div><div><strong>DXF import/export</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Independent reader verifies supported geometry, layers and units.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export and import round-trip a parametric project byte-for-byte when the embedded hash matches, fall back to a warned geometry parse when the file has been edited, reject a file that does not declare units, and warn explicitly that imported vectors are references rather than inferred walls (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: verification is by the application’s own reader, not an independent one, and layer support is limited by the absence of CAD layers (C-06). — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-02 native windows dwg exchange binary file opens independently; unsupported objects are disclosed"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-02</div><div><strong>Native Windows DWG exchange</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Binary file opens independently; unsupported objects are disclosed.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DWG import and export run through a bundled ACadSharp engine with magic-byte validation, a 16 MB cap, cancellation and round-trip verification, and an independent readback verified a 431-entity two-level fixture (`src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: Windows desktop only, other platforms return an explicit unavailable result, and the installed-app path is unverified. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-03 ifc geometry and property exchange declared schema validates with correct object identity"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-03</div><div><strong>IFC geometry and property exchange</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Declared schema validates with correct object identity.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export writes a real ASCII drawing with header units, layer and linetype tables and LINE, LWPOLYLINE, CIRCLE, ARC and TEXT entities, and embeds the parametric project as SHA-256-bound chunks so an unmodified file round-trips to an identical project. A tampered file refuses to restore the stale embedded design and falls back to geometry, and a file that does not declare units is rejected (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: no third-party CAD application has opened the exported file as proof. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-04 bcf issue exchange viewpoint, object references and discussion survive a second application"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-04</div><div><strong>BCF issue exchange</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Viewpoint, object references and discussion survive a second application.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). IFC4 export writes a spatial project, site and building hierarchy with deterministic identifiers and semantic void and fill relationships, asserted at three of each plus a material layer set usage (`src/studio/architect/ifc.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: IFC import does not exist, and no external IFC viewer or checker has validated the file. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-05 landxml and civil exchange alignments, surfaces and units pass independent readback"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-05</div><div><strong>LandXML and civil exchange</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Alignments, surfaces and units pass independent readback.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). LandXML and civil exchange are not implemented. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-06 step, iges and manufacturing exchange declared solids and tolerances survive a second kernel"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-06</div><div><strong>STEP, IGES and manufacturing exchange</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Declared solids and tolerances survive a second kernel.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). STEP, IGES and manufacturing exchange are not implemented. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-07 point-cloud and gis formats las/e57/geojson support is explicit and independently checked"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-07</div><div><strong>Point-cloud and GIS formats</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: LAS/E57/GeoJSON support is explicit and independently checked.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Point-cloud and geographic formats such as LAS, E57 and GeoJSON are not supported. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-08 pdf, image and vector export clipping, scale, fonts and transparency render correctly"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-08</div><div><strong>PDF, image and vector export</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Clipping, scale, fonts and transparency render correctly.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Sheet export produces real vector PDF through a document library rather than a raster capture, and source PDFs render for takeoff with per-page identity (`src/studio/architect/sheets.ts`, `documents.ts`). A five-page PDF was downloaded and inspected in an earlier slice. Remaining: clipping, font embedding and transparency have not been asserted against a reference renderer. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-09 spreadsheet and tabular export column types, escaping and formulas are handled predictably"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-09</div><div><strong>Spreadsheet and tabular export</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Column types, escaping and formulas are handled predictably.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). CSV export escapes cells that begin with a formula character so a spreadsheet cannot execute them, and import refuses mapped formulas even when a cached value is present (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`, `priceWorkbook.ts`; asserted by test). Remaining: column typing on export is not declared, and XLSX is read-only. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-10 referenced file management missing external dependencies are reported before issue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-10</div><div><strong>Referenced file management</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Missing external dependencies are reported before issue.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Missing dependencies are reported rather than silently ignored: backup restore preflight validates originals and reports missing or corrupt assets before any destination read, and the native CAD bridge reports an absent engine as unavailable (`src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts`, `src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: there is no general external-reference manager for linked drawings. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-11 connector authentication provider permissions and token revocation are tested"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-11</div><div><strong>Connector authentication</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Provider permissions and token revocation are tested.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no third-party connectors with user-granted permissions. Provider credentials are server-side environment values with an operator enable flag, not per-user tokens, so permission and revocation testing has no subject. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-12 versioned api and webhooks retries use idempotency and durable acknowledgement"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-12</div><div><strong>Versioned API and webhooks</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Retries use idempotency and durable acknowledgement.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no versioned public interface or webhook delivery, so idempotency and durable acknowledgement cannot be assessed. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-13 import preview and cancellation invalid/cancelled import leaves current project unchanged"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-13</div><div><strong>Import preview and cancellation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Invalid/cancelled import leaves current project unchanged.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A cancelled or invalid import leaves the project unchanged: the CAD bridge supports cancellation tokens, a malformed workbook preserves prior state, and an edited DXF refuses to restore a stale embedded design rather than partially applying it (`src-tauri/src/cad.rs`, `priceWorkbook.ts`, `exchange.ts`). Remaining: there is no import preview step before commit for every format. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="i-14 compatibility and loss reports every conversion lists supported scope and detected losses"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>I-14</div><div><strong>Compatibility and loss reports</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Every conversion lists supported scope and detected losses.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF import reports what it skipped, naming unsupported entity types and bulges, and warns that imported geometry is reference material rather than inferred design (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`). Remaining: DWG, IFC and PDF conversions do not produce a comparable supported-scope and loss report. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-J" data-category="J"><div class="cathead"><h2>J — Jobs, programmes and commercial administration</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.procore.com/project-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Procore Project Management</a> · <a href="https://www.oracle.com/construction-engineering/aconex/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Oracle Aconex</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="j-01 client, site and contact records project links rem