tain condition and cost assumptions.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No operations or asset-management module exists. Asset words refer to project files and media, not to maintained equipment with condition and work orders. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="o-14 decommissioning and disposal retired assets preserve records and disposal evidence"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>O-14</div><div><strong>Decommissioning and disposal</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Retired assets preserve records and disposal evidence.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No operations or asset-management module exists. Asset words refer to project files and media, not to maintained equipment with condition and work orders. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-P" data-category="P"><div class="cathead"><h2>P — Procurement, products and pricing research</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://docs.firecrawl.dev/api-reference/endpoint/search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firecrawl v2 search API</a> · <a href="https://www.rib-software.com/en/rib-costx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RIB CostX</a> · <a href="https://www.procore.com/project-management" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Procore Project Management</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="p-01 user-initiated firecrawl search explicit query returns bounded real source links or honest failure"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-01</div><div><strong>User-initiated Firecrawl search</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Explicit query returns bounded real source links or honest failure.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (live credential); bounded contract implemented in development 2026-09-08: fixed v2 search endpoint, web sources only, at most 5 links, one click starts one attempt, honest typed failures (503 not-configured proven live in the browser; 401/402/429/timeout/cancel/invalid-response/too-large/busy proven with mocked fetch, 27 tests). No live Firecrawl request was made. Code/proof: [SC-04 pricing research](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-pricing-research/README.md). Remaining: real credentialed search with recorded usage, native transport. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-02 supplier and regional filters results show selected country, supplier and search timestamp"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-02</div><div><strong>Supplier and regional filters</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Results show selected country, supplier and search timestamp.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Country, include-only supplier domain and finish timestamp are carried in the result contract and display summary (unit-tested 2026-09-08); no live result has been rendered. Code/proof: [SC-04 pricing research](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-pricing-research/README.md). Remaining: live result, location filter in the UI. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-03 structured product extraction sku, specification, price basis and source excerpt are reviewable"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-03</div><div><strong>Structured product extraction</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: SKU, specification, price basis and source excerpt are reviewable.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). Structured product extraction requires a live search credential that is not configured. The bounded contract returns web sources with a truthful not-configured state, and no scrape or extraction path is implemented (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). A Perplexity route was verified live but is not wired into the product. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-04 variant and product matching different grade/size/finish cannot silently substitute requested item"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-04</div><div><strong>Variant and product matching</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Different grade/size/finish cannot silently substitute requested item.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no product or variant matching, so grade, size and finish substitution cannot be prevented. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-05 price basis and availability ex-tax/inc-tax, pack size, stock and delivery conditions remain explicit"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-05</div><div><strong>Price basis and availability</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Ex-tax/inc-tax, pack size, stock and delivery conditions remain explicit.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Price basis is explicit where rates exist: tax basis, tax percentage, currency, decimals, effective date and supplier are recorded per price book and never inferred (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: pack size, stock and delivery conditions are not modelled, and no researched price carries a basis because research cannot run. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-06 missing and quoted-only prices unknown price remains unknown instead of zero or invented value"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-06</div><div><strong>Missing and quoted-only prices</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Unknown price remains unknown instead of zero or invented value.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unknown price stays unknown rather than becoming zero: the quantity bridge reports an explicit unavailable pricing status per line instead of substituting a value (`src/studio/crmBridge.ts`). Remaining: there is no quoted-only state distinct from unavailable. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-07 price freshness and provenance each rate retains retrieval time, source url and quoted currency"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-07</div><div><strong>Price freshness and provenance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Each rate retains retrieval time, source URL and quoted currency.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). The research contract carries a finish timestamp, the selected country and supplier filters, and duplicate links are collapsed, so a returned rate would keep its retrieval context (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`, `src/studio/pricing/pricingResearch.ts`). Remaining: no live retrieval has occurred, so no rate carries real provenance yet. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-08 review before rate application unreviewed research never changes project costs"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-08</div><div><strong>Review before rate application</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Unreviewed research never changes project costs.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Unreviewed research cannot change project cost because research results are never applied to rates at all: the panel presents candidates and the application path does not exist (`src/studio/pricing/PricingResearchPanel.tsx`). Remaining: this is currently satisfied by absence rather than by a working review gate, so it must be re-assessed when application is built. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-09 provider budgets and credentials secrets remain server/native-only and requests respect limits"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-09</div><div><strong>Provider budgets and credentials</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Secrets remain server/native-only and requests respect limits.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Key read only from server FIRECRAWL_API_KEY with an operator enable flag; never in responses, failures or browser code (tested 2026-09-08); 64 KiB request, 35 s and 1 MiB response caps; single in-flight search; no automatic retry; nominal credit estimate shown separately from reported usage. Code/proof: [SC-04 pricing research](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-pricing-research/README.md). Remaining: durable budget reservation/reconciliation, tenant authorization, native credential store. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-10 search cancellation and retry cancel stops application; rate limits retain existing data"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-10</div><div><strong>Search cancellation and retry</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Cancel stops application; rate limits retain existing data.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Cancel aborts the request and discards late responses; 429 maps to a retryable rate-limited failure; a seeded price book (1 book, 2 rows) stayed byte-identical across a failed search in the browser (2026-09-08); retry requires a fresh click. Code/proof: [SC-04 pricing research](proof/growth/2026-09-08-az3-pricing-research/README.md). Remaining: live provider behaviour, cancel proven against a real in-flight request. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-11 rfq preparation and comparisons supplier offers compare matched scope and exclusions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-11</div><div><strong>RFQ preparation and comparisons</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Supplier offers compare matched scope and exclusions.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Request-for-quotation preparation and offer comparison are not implemented. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-12 purchase orders and approvals only approved quantities/rates enter issued orders"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-12</div><div><strong>Purchase orders and approvals</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Only approved quantities/rates enter issued orders.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Purchase orders and approvals are not implemented. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-13 lead times, alternates and substitutions approved alternative retains original specification and decision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-13</div><div><strong>Lead times, alternates and substitutions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Approved alternative retains original specification and decision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Lead times, alternates and substitutions are not implemented. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="p-14 receiving, returns and reconciliation ordered, delivered, returned and invoiced quantities reconcile"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>P-14</div><div><strong>Receiving, returns and reconciliation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Ordered, delivered, returned and invoiced quantities reconcile.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Receiving, returns and invoice reconciliation are not implemented. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-Q" data-category="Q"><div class="cathead"><h2>Q — Quality, checking, compliance and proof</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/information-delivery-specification-ids/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART IDS</a> · <a href="https://www.csiamerica.com/products/etabs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CSI ETABS</a> · <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="q-01 requirement-to-evidence traceability each acceptance item points to exact fixture and output"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-01</div><div><strong>Requirement-to-evidence traceability</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Each acceptance item points to exact fixture and output.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every assessed row in this register names its code path and its executed test or inspected evidence, and slice records carry commands, results, screenshot paths and fixture digests (walkthrough.md; proof/growth/). Remaining: traceability is maintained by discipline in Markdown rather than enforced by a tool that fails when a row loses its evidence. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-02 smoke tests per delivered change actual screen renders with no uncaught runtime failures"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-02</div><div><strong>Smoke tests per delivered change</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Actual screen renders with no uncaught runtime failures.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every delivered slice runs browser journeys that fail on any uncaught page error, and 1,111 tests across 88 suites with a clean typecheck passed on 2026-09-10. Remaining: smoke coverage is per slice rather than a standing gate over every screen. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-03 screenshot and code-diff proof completed ui row has inspected png plus matching source diff"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-03</div><div><strong>Screenshot and code-diff proof</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Completed UI row has inspected PNG plus matching source diff.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (assessed 2026-09-10). Enforced by harness rather than convention: the repository guardrail hook blocks a completion claim carrying no proof path, and every accepted row in this register cites a code diff plus an executed log or inspected screenshot (`scripts/guardrails/hook.mjs`, `.claude/settings.json`; proof/growth/2026-09-09-guardrails/pipe-tests.log). Reviewed 2026-09-10. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-04 model geometry validation invalid solids, overlaps and missing faces are detected and explained"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-04</div><div><strong>Model geometry validation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Invalid solids, overlaps and missing faces are detected and explained.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Geometry validation rejects invalid solids and explains why: overlapping hosted openings, duplicate physical identity, a fillet radius too large for its segments, and cyclic clipping rings from overlapping return walls are each refused with a stated reason (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`, `precision.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: no general missing-face or manifold check across an imported model. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-05 information requirement checking missing required properties fail the selected rule set"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-05</div><div><strong>Information requirement checking</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Missing required properties fail the selected rule set.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no information-requirement rule set, so missing properties cannot fail a selected standard. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-06 clash and clearance checking known hard and clearance clashes are detected without duplicates"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-06</div><div><strong>Clash and clearance checking</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Known hard and clearance clashes are detected without duplicates.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no clash or clearance checking. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-07 drawing/model/quantity consistency edit updates all linked outputs or marks them stale"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-07</div><div><strong>Drawing/model/quantity consistency</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Edit updates all linked outputs or marks them stale.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Edits mark dependent outputs stale rather than silently diverging: quantity results are re-verified against their operands and job revision, design material sync invalidates a changed review and retires deleted rows, and dimensions and derived views regenerate from the model (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`, `src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`). Remaining: sheets and exported documents are not linked to the model revision they were produced from. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-08 engineering benchmark validation independent known cases verify results and supported range"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-08</div><div><strong>Engineering benchmark validation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Independent known cases verify results and supported range.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no engineering solver, so there are no results to validate against independent known cases. Recorded with the S category. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-09 jurisdiction and edition register every compliance claim identifies applicable published criteria"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-09</div><div><strong>Jurisdiction and edition register</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Every compliance claim identifies applicable published criteria.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No compliance claim is made anywhere in the product, and no jurisdiction or edition register exists. This row stays a gap deliberately rather than being satisfied by silence. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-10 review and professional sign-off checker identity and limitations remain attached to issued result"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-10</div><div><strong>Review and professional sign-off</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Checker identity and limitations remain attached to issued result.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Takeoff evidence is approved for a named person with the approval stamped on the record, and an approval is invalidated when its underlying evidence changes (`src/studio/assistant/takeoffTools.ts`; SC-12 approved a traced run for a named reviewer). Remaining: there is no professional sign-off carrying declared limitations onto an issued output, and without accounts the checker identity is unauthenticated. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-11 evidence integrity and reproducibility hashes bind source, app build, fixture and result"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-11</div><div><strong>Evidence integrity and reproducibility</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Hashes bind source, app build, fixture and result.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Evidence is hash-bound end to end: release stages record frozen source, executable and installer digests, fixtures are hashed, and BOM evidence digests are cross-validated (LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md; proof/growth/2026-09-09-az5-release/). Remaining: reproducing a build from its recorded hashes has not been executed. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-12 regression and adversarial tests malformed files, cancellations and stale edits preserve data"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-12</div><div><strong>Regression and adversarial tests</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Malformed files, cancellations and stale edits preserve data.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Adversarial regressions are executed rather than described: an unsupported schema preserves the original bytes, stale writers are refused, cancelled requests discard late responses, a tampered DXF refuses stale restore, and spreadsheet formulas are never executed on import (`src/studio/persistence.test.ts`, `architect.test.ts`, `src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: coverage is per slice rather than a standing adversarial suite over every store. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-13 release and installed-app verification installed binary and packaged resources match tested build"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-13</div><div><strong>Release and installed-app verification</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Installed binary and packaged resources match tested build.</p><small class="muted">State: failed (assessed 2026-09-10). Not achieved and not achievable in the current process: every verified build runs from an isolated profile and the normal installed application has never been replaced, and an earlier installation attempt stalled on a running process that would not close. Recorded as failed rather than open because the release pipeline currently has no installed-app verification step at all (LATEST-VERIFIED-BUILD.md; DWG-TODO.md). [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">failed</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="q-14 honest capability states planned, partial, failed and verified remain visibly distinct"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Q-14</div><div><strong>Honest capability states</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Planned, partial, failed and verified remain visibly distinct.</p><small class="muted">State: verified (assessed 2026-09-10). This register keeps planned, gap, partial, failed, dependency-blocked and verified visibly distinct, forbids a tick without a code diff plus executed or inspected proof, and states its boundary in each row. Every row was re-assessed against shipping code on 2026-09-10 and stale claims were corrected rather than carried forward. [section 06]</small></div><span class="state">verified</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-R" data-category="R"><div class="cathead"><h2>R — Review, visualization and coordination</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.graphisoft.com/en-us/plans-and-products/archicad-collaborate/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Graphisoft Archicad Collaborate</a> · <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/bim-collaboration-format/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART BCF</a> · <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="r-01 orbit, pan, zoom and fit model remains reachable at different scales and aspect ratios"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-01</div><div><strong>Orbit, pan, zoom and fit</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Model remains reachable at different scales and aspect ratios.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-02 walk and fly navigation movement direction, collision and floor levels match visible controls"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-02</div><div><strong>Walk and fly navigation</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Movement direction, collision and floor levels match visible controls.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-03 section boxes and clipping clipped geometry and caps reveal intended interior sections"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-03</div><div><strong>Section boxes and clipping</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Clipped geometry and caps reveal intended interior sections.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Section cutting produces real plan and section output in the drawing pipeline, but there is no interactive 3D section box or clipping with caps in the viewer, which is what this row requires. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-04 visibility by discipline and phase saved views reproduce selected object sets"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-04</div><div><strong>Visibility by discipline and phase</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Saved views reproduce selected object sets.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Saved views restore camera and display state, and the model viewer separates source reconstructions from a designed model with an explicit status (`src/studio/architect/designedScene.ts`, SC-21). Remaining: there is no visibility control by discipline or phase, so a saved view cannot reproduce a selected object set. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-05 source-linked 3d inspection picked object opens matching source evidence and assumptions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-05</div><div><strong>Source-linked 3D inspection</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Picked object opens matching source evidence and assumptions.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Picked objects carry source identity and evidence state, a designed scene reports no source identity rather than borrowing a catalogue digest, and every reconstruction object is marked inferred with its own digest (`src/studio/SourceBuildingViewer.tsx`, `designedScene.ts`; SC-21 fix). Remaining: opening the matching source page region from a picked object is not proven by an inspected journey. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-06 roof and facade integrity gables join roof slopes without floating faces or hidden duplicate surfaces"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-06</div><div><strong>Roof and facade integrity</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Gables join roof slopes without floating faces or hidden duplicate surfaces.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Roof planes cover the footprint exactly and bear at the wall elevation, gables join intersecting slopes with host cutouts, and fascia and gutter profiles are mitred with finite volume and disappear cleanly when disabled, all asserted by test (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Native visual checks passed in an earlier slice. Remaining: no general duplicate-surface or floating-face detector runs across an arbitrary imported model. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-07 materials, lighting and render views export matches saved camera and material settings"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-07</div><div><strong>Materials, lighting and render views</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Export matches saved camera and material settings.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Material and weather display settings persist and validate, and an AI real-life view renders from the current camera and appears on the render pane with a caption stating its source link status (`src/lib/renderAi.server.ts`; SC-12 and SC-21 journeys). Remaining: rendering is web-only and the native build refuses it, and export matching a saved camera is not asserted. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-08 viewpoint snapshots snapshot retains camera, selection, model revision and annotation"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-08</div><div><strong>Viewpoint snapshots</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Snapshot retains camera, selection, model revision and annotation.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Snapshots record the camera and require a real source identity, and captures are returned to the assistant as evidence (`capture_workspace_image`, recordModelView). Remaining: selection and annotation are not retained in a snapshot. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-09 measurement in 3d picked distance reports coordinates and units with known accuracy"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-09</div><div><strong>Measurement in 3D</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Picked distance reports coordinates and units with known accuracy.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no interactive measurement in the 3D viewer. Measured quantities come from the source-sheet takeoff and the design model, assessed under T rows. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-10 markups and threaded issues issue preserves author, status, due date and model references"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-10</div><div><strong>Markups and threaded issues</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Issue preserves author, status, due date and model references.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Markups and threaded issues in the model are not implemented. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-11 design options and comparisons alternative model changes are inspectable against baseline"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-11</div><div><strong>Design options and comparisons</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Alternative model changes are inspectable against baseline.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Design options and baseline comparison are not implemented. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-12 federated model coordination different origins, versions and disciplines align explicitly"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-12</div><div><strong>Federated model coordination</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Different origins, versions and disciplines align explicitly.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Federated model coordination across origins, versions and disciplines is not implemented. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-13 client presentations and approval viewer comments bind to the exact presented revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-13</div><div><strong>Client presentations and approval</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Viewer comments bind to the exact presented revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Client presentation with comments bound to a presented revision is not implemented. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="r-14 image/video export and accessibility output is legible and controls support keyboard operation"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>R-14</div><div><strong>Image/video export and accessibility</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Output is legible and controls support keyboard operation.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Image export exists through workspace capture and AI render, and the walkthrough and architect surfaces support keyboard operation with reduced-motion handling (`src/studio/shortcuts.ts`; Stage 07 and Stage 09 acceptance). Remaining: video export is limited to recorded QA capture, and no accessibility audit covers the render and review surfaces. [section 02]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-S" data-category="S"><div class="cathead"><h2>S — Structural and specialist engineering</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https