span>S-12</div><div><strong>Bridges, tanks, towers and specialty assets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Selected solver scope explicitly supports the asset type.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No structural or specialist engineering solver exists. Structural appears as a sheet discipline and a takeoff category, and the altitude takeoff explicitly records that structural plans, member schedules, sections and connection details are missing source information rather than computed results. Producing geometry or a quantity never constitutes an engineering solution. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="s-13 fabrication detailing and reinforcement schedules marks, quantities and geometry reconcile issued drawings"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>S-13</div><div><strong>Fabrication detailing and reinforcement schedules</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Marks, quantities and geometry reconcile issued drawings.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No structural or specialist engineering solver exists. Structural appears as a sheet discipline and a takeoff category, and the altitude takeoff explicitly records that structural plans, member schedules, sections and connection details are missing source information rather than computed results. Producing geometry or a quantity never constitutes an engineering solution. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="s-14 calculation reports and check signatures inputs, equations, units, solver version and reviewer are retained"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>S-14</div><div><strong>Calculation reports and check signatures</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Inputs, equations, units, solver version and reviewer are retained.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No structural or specialist engineering solver exists. Structural appears as a sheet discipline and a takeoff category, and the altitude takeoff explicitly records that structural plans, member schedules, sections and connection details are missing source information rather than computed results. Producing geometry or a quantity never constitutes an engineering solution. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-T" data-category="T"><div class="cathead"><h2>T — Takeoff, measurement and quantities</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.rib-software.com/en/rib-costx" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">RIB CostX</a> · <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a> · <a href="https://civilconstruction.trimble.com/en/products/software/trimble-business-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trimble Business Center</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="t-01 scale calibration per sheet known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-01</div><div><strong>Scale calibration per sheet</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Per-sheet calibration converts every supported input unit to metres, round-trips points through a rotated, scaled and translated transform, and is stored per page with duplicate page records rejected and version-1 records migrated (`src/studio/calibration.ts`; `calibration.test.ts`). Remaining: measurement after a deliberate sheet rotation and reload is asserted at transform level, not through an inspected UI journey. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-02 separate axes and distorted scans calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-02</div><div><strong>Separate axes and distorted scans</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Calibration refuses zero-length points, singular transforms and inconsistent converted distances, and records declared, inferred and manual provenance with conflict detection that is independent of candidate order and requires explicit resolution (`src/studio/calibration.ts` reconcileCalibrationCandidates). Remaining: anisotropic separately scaled axes are not represented, so distorted scans are refused rather than measured. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-03 lengths, perimeters and counts totals match independently measured fixture values"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-03</div><div><strong>Lengths, perimeters and counts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Totals match independently measured fixture values.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Length, area, count and sketch measurements exist with tracing runs, gates and topology validation (`src/studio/tracing.ts`, `src/studio/store.ts`; tracing suites pass 2026-09-10). The SC-12 journey traced a run at 5.000 m against a locked 5 m calibration. Remaining: totals are not reconciled against an independently measured fixture across a whole sheet set. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-04 areas, holes and net deductions openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-04</div><div><strong>Areas, holes and net deductions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Area measurement subtracts openings through real polygon boolean geometry, and the architect model proves an opening removes exact material volume once, a T intersection is a union rather than a sum, and overlapping or duplicate hosted openings are rejected (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: net deduction is proven in the design model, not for user-drawn takeoff polygons with holes on a source sheet. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-05 volumes, slopes and elevations 3d quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-05</div><div><strong>Volumes, slopes and elevations</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: 3D quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Volume carries an explicit basis: the area-depth method names its calibration and every depth evidence id, and results are re-verified against their operands and job revision so a stale snapshot is refused (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`). Remaining: projected versus actual sloped surface area is not distinguished, which is the substance of this row. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-06 trade and work-package classification reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-06</div><div><strong>Trade and work-package classification</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Quantities group by trade only. There is no work-package or standard classification such as NRM, Uniclass or CSI, and therefore no reclassification behaviour to assess. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-07 assembly breakdowns element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-07</div><div><strong>Assembly breakdowns</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Element quantities decompose into material rows with declared density, rate revision and waste, and design material sync is idempotent, preserves physical rows, invalidates a changed review and retires deletions (`src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: assumptions are recorded per material rather than presented as a reviewable assembly breakdown. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-08 duplicate detection and exclusions overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-08</div><div><strong>Duplicate detection and exclusions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Overlapping takeoffs are not detected or presented for review before totalling. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-09 revision quantity comparison additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-09</div><div><strong>Revision quantity comparison</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision comparison that reconciles additions, removals and changed quantities against a prior issue. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-10 measurement source links each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-10</div><div><strong>Measurement source links</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every calculation operand requires at least one evidence reference, and document, calibration and photo evidence identity and digests are cross-validated (`src/studio/bomContract.ts`; BOM suites pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: opening the exact page region from a quantity is not proven by an inspected journey. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-11 stock lengths, packs and wastage purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-11</div><div><strong>Stock lengths, packs and wastage</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Waste is applied as a percentage that produces an order quantity distinct from net measured demand on architect wall layers (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts` quantity and cost use net geometry, explicit density, rate revision and waste). Remaining: stock lengths and pack sizes are not modelled, and waste is unavailable on source-sheet takeoff markups. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-12 manual, model and ai quantity provenance user can distinguish and review each quantity origin"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-12</div><div><strong>Manual, model and AI quantity provenance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: User can distinguish and review each quantity origin.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provenance is enforced rather than optional: calibration candidates carry method, evidence and document id, and a candidate with empty evidence is rejected by test. Assistant-created measurements carry tool receipts bound to a revision (SC-12). Remaining: manual, model and AI origins are not surfaced as a single reviewable distinction in the interface. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-13 reconciliation and audit exports summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-13</div><div><strong>Reconciliation and audit exports</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Money totals are summed in integer minor units grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places, so summary figures reproduce their rows without floating-point drift, and CSV export escapes formula-leading cells (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: a reconciliation export that reproduces detailed rows with units and declared rounding is not implemented. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-14 bulk edit, undo and recovery batch operation restores all affected quantities and associations"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-14</div><div><strong>Bulk edit, undo and recovery</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Batch operation restores all affected quantities and associations.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch edit over quantities, and therefore no batch undo or recovery of affected associations. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="t-15 cost code and classification binding every measured item maps to a user-definable classification hierarchy and reports with no unclassified residue"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>T-15</div><div><strong>Cost code and classification binding</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Every measured item maps to a user-definable classification hierarchy and reports with no unclassified residue.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). Added to the register on 2026-09-11 from the quantity surveying specification. T-06 trade and work-package classification is a gap and covers trade grouping; this row covers binding to an extensible cost-code hierarchy so an estimate can be reported, benchmarked and compared between revisions. Without it the whole quantity surveying profile is blocked at its second task. Source: planning/PROPOSED-REGISTER-EXPANSIONS.md. [section 04]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-U" data-category="U"><div class="cathead"><h2>U — Usability, performance and everyday flexibility</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.bluebeam.com/product/markups-and-data/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluebeam markups and data</a> · <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/products/autocad" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk AutoCAD</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="u-01 role-specific workspace presets architect and estimator get useful tools without separate data copies"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-01</div><div><strong>Role-specific workspace presets</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Architect and estimator get useful tools without separate data copies.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Workspaces separate architect, source, model, sheets, pricing and render surfaces over one shared project record, so no role requires a separate data copy (`src/studio/WorkspaceRails.tsx`). Remaining: there are no role presets, and without accounts a role cannot be selected. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-02 search, command palette and shortcuts common commands work from keyboard and show discoverable labels"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-02</div><div><strong>Search, command palette and shortcuts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Common commands work from keyboard and show discoverable labels.</p><small class="muted">State: partial. Navigation milestone verified 2026-09-08; full row remains open. Code/proof: [Stage07 scoped results, source diff and executed evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-07-walkthrough-release/index.html). Latest bounded milestone: [Stage09 clean plans, boundaries, body reach and release evidence](proof/growth/2026-09-08-09-walkthrough-polish/index.html); full row stays open. [section 03]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="u-03 resizable panels and saved layouts layout restores on the user&#39;s monitor without hiding actions"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>U-03</div><div><strong>Resizable panels and saved layouts</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Layout restores on the user&#39;s monitor without hiding actions.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Panels resize and persist: the assistant panel resizes from four corners and can dock into the right rail, the Magic Pencil dock is draggable and clamped back into view on resize, and top menu rows resize with saved layout (`src/studio/assistant/panelCorners.ts`, `draftsmanDockPosition.ts`, `assistantRailMode.ts`; SC-07, SC-14, SC-18). Remaining: layouts are per browser profile and no multi-monitor case is covered. **Defect found 2026-09-11 and fixed 2026-09-12**: opening the architectural workspace collapsed its own container to 236 px, so the authored drawing sheet had a zero-width bounding box and could not be seen or used at any viewport, hiding the sheet, its export control and its properties panel. Cause: the workspace hides the left rail with `display: none` but leaves it in the DOM, so the shared grid in `workspacePanels.css` still matched `:has(&gt; .studio-left-rail)` and reserved a 260 px track for it, placing both children in that track; `architect.css` is imported lazily and lost the `!important` tie 