equirement" data-search="w-14 as-designed versus in-use review operational evidence compares against matching model revision"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>W-14</div><div><strong>As-designed versus in-use review</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Operational evidence compares against matching model revision.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No whole-life performance, sustainability or risk engine exists. There is no energy, carbon, durability or risk model; lifecycle words refer to document and project lifecycles. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed the discipline words in the source are labels and categories, not a validated engine. Any future assessment of this category requires a separately validated solver or a licensed adapter, plus qualified review, per this register’s delivery sequence. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-X" data-category="X"><div class="cathead"><h2>X — Extensibility, automation and AI assistance</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://docs.firecrawl.dev/api-reference/endpoint/search" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Firecrawl v2 search API</a> · <a href="https://www.buildingsmart.org/standards/bsi-standards/information-delivery-specification-ids/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">buildingSMART IDS</a> · <a href="https://www.aveva.com/en/products/unified-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AVEVA Unified Engineering</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="x-01 plugin and adapter boundaries extension failure cannot corrupt the project store"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-01</div><div><strong>Plugin and adapter boundaries</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Extension failure cannot corrupt the project store.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no plugin or adapter boundary, so extension isolation cannot be assessed. The nearest boundary is the native CAD engine subprocess, which is a bundled component rather than a third-party extension. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-02 versioned data schema unsupported schema is rejected with original bytes preserved"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-02</div><div><strong>Versioned data schema</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Unsupported schema is rejected with original bytes preserved.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unsupported project schema version fails closed with a stated expected version and returns the original stored bytes untouched, while a supported legacy version migrates forward, both asserted by test (`src/studio/persistence.ts`; `persistence.test.ts` fails closed for an unknown schema version). The architect store separately proves a future schema cannot be bypassed by ordinary edits. Remaining: no inspected screenshot of the user-facing refusal. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-03 custom workflows and forms organization can add fields and stages without source-code edits"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-03</div><div><strong>Custom workflows and forms</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Organization can add fields and stages without source-code edits.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Custom workflows and forms cannot be defined without source changes. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-04 rules and calculation extensions execution is bounded and results identify rule version"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-04</div><div><strong>Rules and calculation extensions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Execution is bounded and results identify rule version.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no user-supplied rule or calculation extension, so bounded execution and rule versioning cannot be assessed. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-05 batch processing queue jobs are resumable, cancellable and individually diagnosed"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-05</div><div><strong>Batch processing queue</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Jobs are resumable, cancellable and individually diagnosed.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch processing queue with resumable, cancellable, individually diagnosed jobs. Individual long operations are assessed under U-08. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">gap</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-06 ai extraction from source plans suggested object retains exact source region and uncertainty"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-06</div><div><strong>AI extraction from source plans</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Suggested object retains exact source region and uncertainty.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). AI proposals are validated before they touch the design, with bounds, room closure and hosted-door checks and review-time revision binding, so a proposal built against an older revision is refused (`src/studio/architect/layoutAi.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: extraction from a source plan does not retain an exact source region or an uncertainty value, which is the substance of this row. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-07 ai layout/design proposals proposal is separately reviewable before modifying authored design"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-07</div><div><strong>AI layout/design proposals</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Proposal is separately reviewable before modifying authored design.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Proposals cannot silently modify the authored design: validation runs first, the permission mode governs whether an edit executes, and a refusal is returned to the model as a tool error it can read (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`, `useAssistantChat.ts`; permission suite passes 2026-09-10). Remaining: no side-by-side proposal preview before acceptance. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-08 voice and natural-language actions intended edit is understandable and reversible"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-08</div><div><strong>Voice and natural-language actions</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Intended edit is understandable and reversible.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Natural-language actions map to real tools with plain-word intents that never expose raw JSON, and every design edit is undoable through the same history as a manual edit; live journeys drew, edited and undid geometry by entity identifier (SC-08, SC-12, SC-15). Remaining: voice input does not conduct an autonomous conversation. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-09 ai pricing research assistant source evidence accompanies suggested supplier match and rate"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-09</div><div><strong>AI pricing research assistant</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Source evidence accompanies suggested supplier match and rate.</p><small class="muted">State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). The assistant can read price books and import a pasted price book with recorded provenance, but it cannot research a supplier rate because the search credential is not configured and no application path exists (P-03, P-08). Blocked on the same dependency. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24).</small></div><span class="state">dependency-blocked</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-10 tool permission and secret boundaries ai cannot reveal keys or issue unapproved external mutations"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-10</div><div><strong>Tool permission and secret boundaries</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: AI cannot reveal keys or issue unapproved external mutations.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provider keys are read only inside server modules under `src/lib/*.server.ts` and never reach browser code, and unapproved external mutation is blocked by the permission gate: in ask mode no edit tool runs until the user allows it, and a stop denies the pending prompt (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`, 36 tests pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: no adversarial attempt to extract a key through the model has been executed. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-11 usage limits and cost reporting provider usage is capped and reported per operation"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-11</div><div><strong>Usage limits and cost reporting</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Provider usage is capped and reported per operation.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Usage is estimated and reported as a context meter with a hard stop at the declared budget, folding in provider caps on entries, images and request bytes (`src/studio/assistant/contextBudget.ts`). Remaining: per-operation monetary cost is not reported, and the estimate is a client-side approximation rather than provider-reported usage. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-12 human review and rejection rejected proposal leaves authoritative design unchanged"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-12</div><div><strong>Human review and rejection</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Rejected proposal leaves authoritative design unchanged.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A denied permission prompt leaves the design unchanged and returns an explicit refusal rather than failing silently, asserted across allow once, allow for this chat, deny and stop (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`). Remaining: rejecting an already-applied change relies on undo rather than a proposal queue. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-13 automation provenance prompt/input version, tool and accepted changes are traceable"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-13</div><div><strong>Automation provenance</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Prompt/input version, tool and accepted changes are traceable.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Work packets persist the objective, the actions taken and the raw task events, and tool receipts are bound to the design revision they changed (`src/studio/assistant/workPacket.ts`, `workPacketStore.ts`). Remaining: the prompt or manual version in force is not recorded alongside the accepted changes. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article><article class="requirement" data-search="x-14 integration health and retries unavailable service is visible and retry does not duplicate work"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>X-14</div><div><strong>Integration health and retries</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Unavailable service is visible and retry does not duplicate work.</p><small class="muted">State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unconfigured or failing provider is reported truthfully rather than hidden: the pricing route distinguishes not-configured, 401, 402, 429, timeout, abort, oversized and malformed responses, and single-flight refusal prevents a duplicate in-flight request (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: there is no automatic retry policy, so retry without duplication is proven only for the refusal path. [section 05]</small></div><span class="state">partial</span></article></section><section class="category" id="category-Y" data-category="Y"><div class="cathead"><h2>Y — Yards, infrastructure, industrial and specialist assets</h2><p class="benchmarks">Benchmarks: <a href="https://www.autodesk.com/uk/products/civil-3d/features" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Autodesk Civil 3D</a> · <a href="https://www.aveva.com/en/products/unified-engineering/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">AVEVA Unified Engineering</a> · <a href="https://civilconstruction.trimble.com/en/products/software/trimble-business-center" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Trimble Business Center</a>. Requirements below are X-Ray targets.</p></div><article class="requirement" data-search="y-01 road alignments and corridors stationing, profiles and sections reconcile corridor geometry"><div class="reqid"><span class="check" aria-label="Unchecked"></span>Y-01</div><div><strong>Road alignments and corridors</strong><p class="acceptance">Pass when: Stationing, profiles and sections reconcile corridor geometry.</p><small class="muted">State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). No yards, infrastructure or industrial-asset module exists. These specialist asset types have no representation in the data model. Recorded as a gap on 2026-09-10 after a code search confirmed t