-"I-08","Interoperability, imports and integrations","PDF, image and vector export","Clipping, scale, fonts and transparency render correctly","partial","src/studio/architect/sheets.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Sheet export produces real vector PDF through a document library rather than a raster capture, and source PDFs render for takeoff with per-page identity (`src/studio/architect/sheets.ts`, `documents.ts`). A five-page PDF was downloaded and inspected in an earlier slice. Remaining: clipping, font embedding and transparency have not been asserted against a reference renderer."
-"I-09","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Spreadsheet and tabular export","Column types, escaping and formulas are handled predictably","partial","src/studio/priceBooks.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). CSV export escapes cells that begin with a formula character so a spreadsheet cannot execute them, and import refuses mapped formulas even when a cached value is present (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`, `priceWorkbook.ts`; asserted by test). Remaining: column typing on export is not declared, and XLSX is read-only."
-"I-10","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Referenced file management","Missing external dependencies are reported before issue","partial","src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts; src/cad.rs","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Missing dependencies are reported rather than silently ignored: backup restore preflight validates originals and reports missing or corrupt assets before any destination read, and the native CAD bridge reports an absent engine as unavailable (`src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts`, `src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: there is no general external-reference manager for linked drawings."
-"I-11","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Connector authentication","Provider permissions and token revocation are tested","dependency-blocked","","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no third-party connectors with user-granted permissions. Provider credentials are server-side environment values with an operator enable flag, not per-user tokens, so permission and revocation testing has no subject."
