+"C-09","CAD precision and drawing tools","Offset, trim, extend and fillet","Edge cases retain valid connected geometry","partial","src/studio/architect/precision.ts","","ACAD","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Offset, mirror, trim, extend and a tangential fillet are real solvers with asserted results and explicit edge-case refusals: a radius too large for its segments, parallel segments that cannot meet, and an intersection already inside the segment are each rejected with a stated reason (`src/studio/architect/precision.ts`; `architect.test.ts` ""precision exact length, mirror, offset, trim, extend and tangential fillet""). Remaining: no inspected screenshot, and connected-geometry survival is proven per operation rather than across a drawing session. [section 02]"
