+"I-01","Interoperability, imports and integrations","DXF import/export","Independent reader verifies supported geometry, layers and units","partial","src/studio/architect/exchange.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export and import round-trip a parametric project byte-for-byte when the embedded hash matches, fall back to a warned geometry parse when the file has been edited, reject a file that does not declare units, and warn explicitly that imported vectors are references rather than inferred walls (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: verification is by the application’s own reader, not an independent one, and layer support is limited by the absence of CAD layers (C-06). — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-02","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Native Windows DWG exchange","Binary file opens independently; unsupported objects are disclosed","partial","src/cad.rs","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DWG import and export run through a bundled ACadSharp engine with magic-byte validation, a 16 MB cap, cancellation and round-trip verification, and an independent readback verified a 431-entity two-level fixture (`src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: Windows desktop only, other platforms return an explicit unavailable result, and the installed-app path is unverified. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-03","Interoperability, imports and integrations","IFC geometry and property exchange","Declared schema validates with correct object identity","partial","src/studio/architect/exchange.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export writes a real ASCII drawing with header units, layer and linetype tables and LINE, LWPOLYLINE, CIRCLE, ARC and TEXT entities, and embeds the parametric project as SHA-256-bound chunks so an unmodified file round-trips to an identical project. A tampered file refuses to restore the stale embedded design and falls back to geometry, and a file that does not declare units is rejected (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: no third-party CAD application has opened the exported file as proof. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-04","Interoperability, imports and integrations","BCF issue exchange","Viewpoint, object references and discussion survive a second application","partial","src/studio/architect/ifc.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). IFC4 export writes a spatial project, site and building hierarchy with deterministic identifiers and semantic void and fill relationships, asserted at three of each plus a material layer set usage (`src/studio/architect/ifc.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: IFC import does not exist, and no external IFC viewer or checker has validated the file. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-05","Interoperability, imports and integrations","LandXML and civil exchange","Alignments, surfaces and units pass independent readback","gap","","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). LandXML and civil exchange are not implemented. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-06","Interoperability, imports and integrations","STEP, IGES and manufacturing exchange","Declared solids and tolerances survive a second kernel","gap","","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). STEP, IGES and manufacturing exchange are not implemented. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-07","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Point-cloud and GIS formats","LAS/E57/GeoJSON support is explicit and independently checked","gap","","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Point-cloud and geographic formats such as LAS, E57 and GeoJSON are not supported. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-08","Interoperability, imports and integrations","PDF, image and vector export","Clipping, scale, fonts and transparency render correctly","partial","src/studio/architect/sheets.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Sheet export produces real vector PDF through a document library rather than a raster capture, and source PDFs render for takeoff with per-page identity (`src/studio/architect/sheets.ts`, `documents.ts`). A five-page PDF was downloaded and inspected in an earlier slice. Remaining: clipping, font embedding and transparency have not been asserted against a reference renderer. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-09","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Spreadsheet and tabular export","Column types, escaping and formulas are handled predictably","partial","src/studio/priceBooks.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). CSV export escapes cells that begin with a formula character so a spreadsheet cannot execute them, and import refuses mapped formulas even when a cached value is present (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`, `priceWorkbook.ts`; asserted by test). Remaining: column typing on export is not declared, and XLSX is read-only. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-10","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Referenced file management","Missing external dependencies are reported before issue","partial","src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts; src/cad.rs","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Missing dependencies are reported rather than silently ignored: backup restore preflight validates originals and reports missing or corrupt assets before any destination read, and the native CAD bridge reports an absent engine as unavailable (`src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts`, `src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: there is no general external-reference manager for linked drawings. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-11","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Connector authentication","Provider permissions and token revocation are tested","dependency-blocked","","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no third-party connectors with user-granted permissions. Provider credentials are server-side environment values with an operator enable flag, not per-user tokens, so permission and revocation testing has no subject. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-12","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Versioned API and webhooks","Retries use idempotency and durable acknowledgement","gap","","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no versioned public interface or webhook delivery, so idempotency and durable acknowledgement cannot be assessed. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-13","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Import preview and cancellation","Invalid/cancelled import leaves current project unchanged","partial","src/cad.rs","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A cancelled or invalid import leaves the project unchanged: the CAD bridge supports cancellation tokens, a malformed workbook preserves prior state, and an edited DXF refuses to restore a stale embedded design rather than partially applying it (`src-tauri/src/cad.rs`, `priceWorkbook.ts`, `exchange.ts`). Remaining: there is no import preview step before commit for every format. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"I-14","Interoperability, imports and integrations","Compatibility and loss reports","Every conversion lists supported scope and detected losses","partial","src/studio/architect/exchange.ts","","ACAD; DWG; BCF; IDS","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF import reports what it skipped, naming unsupported entity types and bulges, and warns that imported geometry is reference material rather than inferred design (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`). Remaining: DWG, IFC and PDF conversions do not produce a comparable supported-scope and loss report. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
