+"T-01","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Scale calibration per sheet","Known distance measures correctly after rotation and reload","partial","src/studio/calibration.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Per-sheet calibration converts every supported input unit to metres, round-trips points through a rotated, scaled and translated transform, and is stored per page with duplicate page records rejected and version-1 records migrated (`src/studio/calibration.ts`; `calibration.test.ts`). Remaining: measurement after a deliberate sheet rotation and reload is asserted at transform level, not through an inspected UI journey. [section 04]"
+"T-02","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Separate axes and distorted scans","Calibration records anisotropy or blocks unsupported measurement","partial","src/studio/calibration.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Calibration refuses zero-length points, singular transforms and inconsistent converted distances, and records declared, inferred and manual provenance with conflict detection that is independent of candidate order and requires explicit resolution (`src/studio/calibration.ts` reconcileCalibrationCandidates). Remaining: anisotropic separately scaled axes are not represented, so distorted scans are refused rather than measured. [section 04]"
+"T-03","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Lengths, perimeters and counts","Totals match independently measured fixture values","partial","src/studio/tracing.ts; src/studio/store.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Length, area, count and sketch measurements exist with tracing runs, gates and topology validation (`src/studio/tracing.ts`, `src/studio/store.ts`; tracing suites pass 2026-09-10). The SC-12 journey traced a run at 5.000 m against a locked 5 m calibration. Remaining: totals are not reconciled against an independently measured fixture across a whole sheet set. [section 04]"
+"T-04","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Areas, holes and net deductions","Openings subtract once and self-intersections are rejected","partial","src/studio/architect/geometry.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Area measurement subtracts openings through real polygon boolean geometry, and the architect model proves an opening removes exact material volume once, a T intersection is a union rather than a sum, and overlapping or duplicate hosted openings are rejected (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: net deduction is proven in the design model, not for user-drawn takeoff polygons with holes on a source sheet. [section 04]"
+"T-05","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Volumes, slopes and elevations","3D quantity basis distinguishes projected from actual surface","partial","src/studio/construction/quantity.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Volume carries an explicit basis: the area-depth method names its calibration and every depth evidence id, and results are re-verified against their operands and job revision so a stale snapshot is refused (`src/studio/construction/quantity.ts`). Remaining: projected versus actual sloped surface area is not distinguished, which is the substance of this row. [section 04]"
+"T-06","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Trade and work-package classification","Reclassification updates totals without duplicate measurements","gap","","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Quantities group by trade only. There is no work-package or standard classification such as NRM, Uniclass or CSI, and therefore no reclassification behaviour to assess. [section 04]"
+"T-07","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Assembly breakdowns","Element quantity decomposes into explicit materials and assumptions","partial","src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Element quantities decompose into material rows with declared density, rate revision and waste, and design material sync is idempotent, preserves physical rows, invalidates a changed review and retires deletions (`src/studio/architect/materialBridge.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: assumptions are recorded per material rather than presented as a reviewable assembly breakdown. [section 04]"
+"T-08","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Duplicate detection and exclusions","Overlapping takeoffs are reviewable before totaling","gap","","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Overlapping takeoffs are not detected or presented for review before totalling. [section 04]"
+"T-09","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Revision quantity comparison","Additions, removals and changed quantities reconcile prior issue","gap","","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no revision comparison that reconciles additions, removals and changed quantities against a prior issue. [section 04]"
+"T-10","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Measurement source links","Each quantity opens exact page, region and source revision","partial","src/studio/bomContract.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Every calculation operand requires at least one evidence reference, and document, calibration and photo evidence identity and digests are cross-validated (`src/studio/bomContract.ts`; BOM suites pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: opening the exact page region from a quantity is not proven by an inspected journey. [section 04]"
+"T-11","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Stock lengths, packs and wastage","Purchased quantities remain distinct from net measured demand","partial","src/studio/architect/geometry.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Waste is applied as a percentage that produces an order quantity distinct from net measured demand on architect wall layers (`src/studio/architect/geometry.ts`; `architect.test.ts` quantity and cost use net geometry, explicit density, rate revision and waste). Remaining: stock lengths and pack sizes are not modelled, and waste is unavailable on source-sheet takeoff markups. [section 04]"
+"T-12","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Manual, model and AI quantity provenance","User can distinguish and review each quantity origin","partial","","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provenance is enforced rather than optional: calibration candidates carry method, evidence and document id, and a candidate with empty evidence is rejected by test. Assistant-created measurements carry tool receipts bound to a revision (SC-12). Remaining: manual, model and AI origins are not surfaced as a single reviewable distinction in the interface. [section 04]"
+"T-13","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Reconciliation and audit exports","Summary totals reproduce detailed rows with units and rounding","partial","src/studio/priceBooks.ts","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Money totals are summed in integer minor units grouped by currency, tax basis and decimal places, so summary figures reproduce their rows without floating-point drift, and CSV export escapes formula-leading cells (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`). Remaining: a reconciliation export that reproduces detailed rows with units and declared rounding is not implemented. [section 04]"
+"T-14","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Bulk edit, undo and recovery","Batch operation restores all affected quantities and associations","gap","","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch edit over quantities, and therefore no batch undo or recovery of affected associations. [section 04]"
+"T-15","Takeoff, measurement and quantities","Cost code and classification binding","Every measured item maps to a user-definable classification hierarchy and reports with no unclassified residue","gap","","","COSTX; BLUEBEAM; TRIMBLE","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-11). Added to the register on 2026-09-11 from the quantity surveying specification. T-06 trade and work-package classification is a gap and covers trade grouping; this row covers binding to an extensible cost-code hierarchy so an estimate can be reported, benchmarked and compared between revisions. Without it the whole quantity surveying profile is blocked at its second task. Source: planning/PROPOSED-REGISTER-EXPANSIONS.md. [section 04]"
+"U-01","Usability, performance and everyday flexibility","Role-specific workspace presets","Architect and estimator get useful tools without separate data copies","partial","src/studio/WorkspaceRails.tsx","","BLUEBEAM; ACAD","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Workspaces separate architect, source, model, sheets, pricing and render surfaces over one shared project record, so no role requires a separate data copy (`src/studio/WorkspaceRails.tsx`). Remaining: there are no role presets, and without accounts a role cannot be selected. [section 03]"
