+"U-03","Usability, performance and everyday flexibility","Resizable panels and saved layouts","Layout restores on the user's monitor without hiding actions","partial","src/studio/assistant/panelCorners.ts; src/studio/architect/architect.css","proof/growth/2026-09-12-u03-workspace-width/README.md; proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md","BLUEBEAM; ACAD","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Panels resize and persist: the assistant panel resizes from four corners and can dock into the right rail, the Magic Pencil dock is draggable and clamped back into view on resize, and top menu rows resize with saved layout (`src/studio/assistant/panelCorners.ts`, `draftsmanDockPosition.ts`, `assistantRailMode.ts`; SC-07, SC-14, SC-18). Remaining: layouts are per browser profile and no multi-monitor case is covered. **Defect found 2026-09-11 and fixed 2026-09-12**: opening the architectural workspace collapsed its own container to 236 px, so the authored drawing sheet had a zero-width bounding box and could not be seen or used at any viewport, hiding the sheet, its export control and its properties panel. Cause: the workspace hides the left rail with `display: none` but leaves it in the DOM, so the shared grid in `workspacePanels.css` still matched `:has(> .studio-left-rail)` and reserved a 260 px track for it, placing both children in that track; `architect.css` is imported lazily and lost the `!important` tie on stylesheet order. Fixed by raising selector specificity in `src/studio/architect/architect.css`. Verified in the browser: grid `260px 1420px` with main at 236 px becomes `1280px 400px` with main at 1280 px, the sheet renders at 973x688 (was 0x0), and the four main panes plus the sketch pane's other mode keep their existing widths. Inspected screenshots at 1680x1050 show the working workspace and, for the first time in situ, the D-07 title block. Evidence: proof/growth/2026-09-12-u03-workspace-width/README.md. Remaining beyond this row's existing items: the shared grid still sizes itself from a hidden element's presence in the DOM, so another workspace hiding a rail would hit the same trap; and no tablet capture. Review follow-up 2026-09-12: Settings seam/resize controls, assistant handover and saved Visual settings width are implemented; full browser interaction verification is pending a test-host blocker. See proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md. This row remains partial. Review follow-up 2026-09-12: Settings seam/resize controls, assistant handover and saved Visual settings width are implemented; full browser interaction verification is pending a test-host blocker. See proof/growth/2026-09-12-visualise-review/README.md. This row remains partial. [section 03]"
