+"X-01","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Plugin and adapter boundaries","Extension failure cannot corrupt the project store","gap","","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no plugin or adapter boundary, so extension isolation cannot be assessed. The nearest boundary is the native CAD engine subprocess, which is a bundled component rather than a third-party extension. [section 05]"
+"X-02","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Versioned data schema","Unsupported schema is rejected with original bytes preserved","partial","src/studio/persistence.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unsupported project schema version fails closed with a stated expected version and returns the original stored bytes untouched, while a supported legacy version migrates forward, both asserted by test (`src/studio/persistence.ts`; `persistence.test.ts` fails closed for an unknown schema version). The architect store separately proves a future schema cannot be bypassed by ordinary edits. Remaining: no inspected screenshot of the user-facing refusal. [section 05]"
+"X-03","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Custom workflows and forms","Organization can add fields and stages without source-code edits","gap","","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Custom workflows and forms cannot be defined without source changes. [section 05]"
+"X-04","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Rules and calculation extensions","Execution is bounded and results identify rule version","gap","","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no user-supplied rule or calculation extension, so bounded execution and rule versioning cannot be assessed. [section 05]"
+"X-05","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Batch processing queue","Jobs are resumable, cancellable and individually diagnosed","gap","","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). There is no batch processing queue with resumable, cancellable, individually diagnosed jobs. Individual long operations are assessed under U-08. [section 05]"
+"X-06","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","AI extraction from source plans","Suggested object retains exact source region and uncertainty","partial","src/studio/architect/layoutAi.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). AI proposals are validated before they touch the design, with bounds, room closure and hosted-door checks and review-time revision binding, so a proposal built against an older revision is refused (`src/studio/architect/layoutAi.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: extraction from a source plan does not retain an exact source region or an uncertainty value, which is the substance of this row. [section 05]"
+"X-07","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","AI layout/design proposals","Proposal is separately reviewable before modifying authored design","partial","src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Proposals cannot silently modify the authored design: validation runs first, the permission mode governs whether an edit executes, and a refusal is returned to the model as a tool error it can read (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`, `useAssistantChat.ts`; permission suite passes 2026-09-10). Remaining: no side-by-side proposal preview before acceptance. [section 05]"
+"X-08","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Voice and natural-language actions","Intended edit is understandable and reversible","partial","","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Natural-language actions map to real tools with plain-word intents that never expose raw JSON, and every design edit is undoable through the same history as a manual edit; live journeys drew, edited and undid geometry by entity identifier (SC-08, SC-12, SC-15). Remaining: voice input does not conduct an autonomous conversation. [section 05]"
+"X-09","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","AI pricing research assistant","Source evidence accompanies suggested supplier match and rate","dependency-blocked","","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). The assistant can read price books and import a pasted price book with recorded provenance, but it cannot research a supplier rate because the search credential is not configured and no application path exists (P-03, P-08). Blocked on the same dependency. — moved to POST-V1-BACKLOG (v1 scope freeze 2026-09-24)."
+"X-10","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Tool permission and secret boundaries","AI cannot reveal keys or issue unapproved external mutations","partial","src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Provider keys are read only inside server modules under `src/lib/*.server.ts` and never reach browser code, and unapproved external mutation is blocked by the permission gate: in ask mode no edit tool runs until the user allows it, and a stop denies the pending prompt (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`, 36 tests pass 2026-09-10). Remaining: no adversarial attempt to extract a key through the model has been executed. [section 05]"
+"X-11","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Usage limits and cost reporting","Provider usage is capped and reported per operation","partial","src/studio/assistant/contextBudget.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Usage is estimated and reported as a context meter with a hard stop at the declared budget, folding in provider caps on entries, images and request bytes (`src/studio/assistant/contextBudget.ts`). Remaining: per-operation monetary cost is not reported, and the estimate is a client-side approximation rather than provider-reported usage. [section 05]"
+"X-12","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Human review and rejection","Rejected proposal leaves authoritative design unchanged","partial","src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). A denied permission prompt leaves the design unchanged and returns an explicit refusal rather than failing silently, asserted across allow once, allow for this chat, deny and stop (`src/studio/assistant/permissions.ts`). Remaining: rejecting an already-applied change relies on undo rather than a proposal queue. [section 05]"
+"X-13","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Automation provenance","Prompt/input version, tool and accepted changes are traceable","partial","src/studio/assistant/workPacket.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Work packets persist the objective, the actions taken and the raw task events, and tool receipts are bound to the design revision they changed (`src/studio/assistant/workPacket.ts`, `workPacketStore.ts`). Remaining: the prompt or manual version in force is not recorded alongside the accepted changes. [section 05]"
+"X-14","Extensibility, automation and AI assistance","Integration health and retries","Unavailable service is visible and retry does not duplicate work","partial","src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts","","FIRECRAWL; IDS; AVEVA","no","State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). An unconfigured or failing provider is reported truthfully rather than hidden: the pricing route distinguishes not-configured, 401, 402, 429, timeout, abort, oversized and malformed responses, and single-flight refusal prevents a duplicate in-flight request (`src/lib/pricingResearch.server.ts`). Remaining: there is no automatic retry policy, so retry without duplication is proven only for the refusal path. [section 05]"
