+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:245](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L245) — **I-01 DXF import/export** — Independent reader verifies supported geometry, layers and units. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export and import round-trip a parametric project byte-for-byte when the embedded hash matches, fall back to a warned geometry parse when the file has been edited, reject a file that does not declare units, and warn explicitly that imported vectors are references rather than inferred walls (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: verification is by the application’s own reader, not an independent one, and layer support is limited by the absence of CAD layers (C-06).
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:246](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L246) — **I-02 Native Windows DWG exchange** — Binary file opens independently; unsupported objects are disclosed. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DWG import and export run through a bundled ACadSharp engine with magic-byte validation, a 16 MB cap, cancellation and round-trip verification, and an independent readback verified a 431-entity two-level fixture (`src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: Windows desktop only, other platforms return an explicit unavailable result, and the installed-app path is unverified.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:247](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L247) — **I-03 IFC geometry and property exchange** — Declared schema validates with correct object identity. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). DXF export writes a real ASCII drawing with header units, layer and linetype tables and LINE, LWPOLYLINE, CIRCLE, ARC and TEXT entities, and embeds the parametric project as SHA-256-bound chunks so an unmodified file round-trips to an identical project. A tampered file refuses to restore the stale embedded design and falls back to geometry, and a file that does not declare units is rejected (`src/studio/architect/exchange.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: no third-party CAD application has opened the exported file as proof.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:248](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L248) — **I-04 BCF issue exchange** — Viewpoint, object references and discussion survive a second application. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). IFC4 export writes a spatial project, site and building hierarchy with deterministic identifiers and semantic void and fill relationships, asserted at three of each plus a material layer set usage (`src/studio/architect/ifc.ts`; `architect.test.ts`). Remaining: IFC import does not exist, and no external IFC viewer or checker has validated the file.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:249](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L249) — **I-05 LandXML and civil exchange** — Alignments, surfaces and units pass independent readback. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). LandXML and civil exchange are not implemented.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:250](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L250) — **I-06 STEP, IGES and manufacturing exchange** — Declared solids and tolerances survive a second kernel. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). STEP, IGES and manufacturing exchange are not implemented.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:251](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L251) — **I-07 Point-cloud and GIS formats** — LAS/E57/GeoJSON support is explicit and independently checked. State: gap (assessed 2026-09-10). Point-cloud and geographic formats such as LAS, E57 and GeoJSON are not supported.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:252](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L252) — **I-08 PDF, image and vector export** — Clipping, scale, fonts and transparency render correctly. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Sheet export produces real vector PDF through a document library rather than a raster capture, and source PDFs render for takeoff with per-page identity (`src/studio/architect/sheets.ts`, `documents.ts`). A five-page PDF was downloaded and inspected in an earlier slice. Remaining: clipping, font embedding and transparency have not been asserted against a reference renderer.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:253](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L253) — **I-09 Spreadsheet and tabular export** — Column types, escaping and formulas are handled predictably. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). CSV export escapes cells that begin with a formula character so a spreadsheet cannot execute them, and import refuses mapped formulas even when a cached value is present (`src/studio/priceBooks.ts`, `priceWorkbook.ts`; asserted by test). Remaining: column typing on export is not declared, and XLSX is read-only.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:254](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L254) — **I-10 Referenced file management** — Missing external dependencies are reported before issue. State: partial (assessed 2026-09-10). Missing dependencies are reported rather than silently ignored: backup restore preflight validates originals and reports missing or corrupt assets before any destination read, and the native CAD bridge reports an absent engine as unavailable (`src/studio/backupRestorePreflight.ts`, `src-tauri/src/cad.rs`). Remaining: there is no general external-reference manager for linked drawings.
+- [PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md:255](PROFESSIONAL-A-Z-CHECKLIST.md#L255) — **I-11 Connector authentication** — Provider permissions and token revocation are tested. State: dependency-blocked (assessed 2026-09-10). There are no third-party connectors with user-granted permissions. Provider credentials are server-side environment values with an operator enable flag, not per-user tokens, so permission and revocation testing has no subject.
